{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c535","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0798e-8ce3-71d2-82cf-4115ffc6a2dc"},"sequence":245,"recorded_at":1780531400000485,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a27566c0-e07d-4374-b9c6-044054a3f322"},"task_id":"a27566c0-e07d-4374-b9c6-044054a3f322","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"a27566c0-e07d-4374-b9c6-044054a3f322","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`.\n1|// AST-derived refusal-arm inventory for the terminal backend packages.\n2|//\n3|// The failure this file exists to prevent: a brand-new production refusal\n4|// arm carrying a brand-new unasserted detail shipped while `gofmt`,\n5|// `go vet`, `go test ./...`, and `tracecheck` all stayed green. A\n6|// hand-maintained arm list cannot catch that; a derived one can, but only\n7|// if it is checked in BOTH directions. The forward direction alone passes\n8|// vacuously on a truncated derivation: every derived arm asserted is true\n9|// when the derivation silently dropped half the package. So this file\n10|// derives every refusal arm from the production AST, requires each to\n11|// resolve to exactly one declared row naming a real asserting test, and\n12|// requires every declared row to resolve to exactly one derived arm.\n13|//\n14|// Modelled on internal/canonicaljson/grammar_inventory_test.go: derivation\n15|// fails closed on an empty, short, or unparseable input, and the declared\n16|// table cannot move its own goalposts because the derivation never\n17|// consults it.\n18|//\n19|// Stated bounds (not inferred):\n20|//   - The inventory proves every arm is DECLARED with a resolving test.\n21|//     Execution and decision proof is each row's named test, measured by\n22|//     this package's suite. A row resolves textually (detail mention, or\n23|//     entry-plus-code/predicate mention); a wrongly attributed row that\n24|//     still resolves is a review finding, not a green light.\n25|//   - Attribution drift survives through that fallback: a\n26|//     dead-by-construction arm can resolve through a sibling site's test\n27|//     while pointing at the wrong guard. Live example: CheckTransition's\n28|//     \"operation vocabulary\" arm (conformance.go) is unreachable —\n29|//     ParseOperation admits exactly the ten operations transitionTable\n30|//     covers, so lookupTransition never misses — yet the row carries no\n31|//     bound and resolves through TestParseOperationAdmitsOnlyTheTenClosedOperations,\n32|//     which drives ParseOperation's own arm sharing the detail. The five\n33|//     re-parse arms are the contrast: they declare boundDefensiveReparse\n34|//     and TestDefensiveBoundsAreExactlyThese pins the set.\n35|//   - Kill inflation: both inventory directions fail on ANY added or\n36|//     deleted production arm by construction, so an arm-deleting mutant\n37|//     elsewhere reads as killed by the inventory alone with no behavioral\n38|//     change. Mutation scores measured with this file present are NOT\n39|//     comparable to pre-inventory scores; review the failing-test list,\n40|//     not just the exit code.\n41|//   - errors.New/fmt.Errorf sites are not wire refusals and carry no arm.\n42|//     They live only in validatePlatforms (funneled into one *Error arm\n43|//     whose detail set is pinned exactly) and DigestFile (I/O errors that\n44|//     must never be *Error). Both properties are asserted below, in every\n45|//     FuncDecl body plus every package-level var initializer, and any\n46|//     reference to either constructor outside direct-call position\n47|//     (e.g. `newPlain := errors.New`) fails the suite, so an aliased\n48|//     construction cannot ship unattributed.\n49|//   - The DigestFile half of that allowlist is function-wide with no\n50|//     detail pin, unlike validatePlatforms' derived exact set: a new\n51|//     errors.New on any path inside DigestFile passes the gate (and the\n52|//     never-wire behavioral assertion, which only drives the current\n53|//     paths). Disclosed, not closed.\n54|//   - Custom error types outside the two recognised spellings (*Error,\n55|//     errors.New, fmt.Errorf) are outside both derivations: a bespoke\n56|//     error type smuggled as a refusal survives. Disclosed, not closed.\n57|//   - Constructor Details are single static literals by assertion: the\n58|//     derivation fatals on any mismatchf/integrityFailure call without\n59|//     exactly one string-literal argument, so format-verb interpolation\n60|//     cannot enter the table. Zero multi-argument sites today; go vet's\n61|//     printf analyzer independently refuses a non-constant format string.\n62|package terminalbackend\n63|\n64|import (\n65|\t\"errors\"\n66|\t\"go/ast\"\n67|\t\"go/parser\"\n68|\t\"go/token\"\n69|\t\"os\"\n70|\t\"path/filepath\"\n71|\t\"strconv\"\n72|\t\"strings\"\n73|\t\"testing\"\n74|)\n75|\n76|// refusalArm is one derived production refusal: a wire-code *Error\n77|// construction site keyed by file, enclosing function (receiver-qualified\n78|// for methods), code symbol, static detail, and occurrence index within\n79|// that key. The index keeps two identical arms in one function distinct:\n80|// adding a second arm with an already-declared key fails on the missing\n81|// #2 row instead of hiding behind #1.\n82|type refusalArm struct {\n83|\tfile       string\n84|\tfunction   string\n85|\tcode       string\n86|\tdetail     string\n87|\toccurrence int\n88|}\n89|\n90|// constructorFunctions build refusals instead of issuing them. Their own\n91|// *Error sites are the funnel, not arms.\n92|var constructorFunctions = map[string]bool{\n93|\t\"mismatchf\":        true,\n94|\t\"integrityFailure\": true,\n95|}\n96|\n97|// passthroughDetail marks the single dynamic-detail funnel: Registration\n98|// validation wraps validatePlatforms errors via err.Error(). Every other\n99|// Detail expression must be a static string literal; a new dynamic detail\n100|// fails the derivation rather than entering the table silently.\n101|const passthroughDetail = \"passthrough:err.Error()\"\n102|\n103|// deriveRefusalArms walks every production file of this package (every\n104|// *.go except *_test.go, so a new production file is scanned without\n105|// anyone remembering it) and returns every refusal arm in source order.\n106|// It fails closed: an unparseable file, a non-static code or detail, and\n107|// an empty result are all fatal, never an empty table.\n108|//\n109|// Coverage is declaration-complete, not FuncDecl-complete: every FuncDecl\n110|// body (including nested func literals, methods, and init) plus every\n111|// package-level var initializer is scanned, so a refusal arm hiding in a\n112|// package-level `var f = func() *Error {...}` is derived like any other.\n113|// Constructor references outside direct-call position (`refuse :=\n114|// mismatchf`) are rejected outright by rejectConstructorAliases below:\n115|// an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, so it fails the suite rather\n116|// than shipping silently.\n117|func deriveRefusalArms(t *testing.T) []refusalArm {\n118|\tt.Helper()\n119|\n120|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n121|\tif err != nil {\n122|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n123|\t}\n124|\tvar production []string\n125|\tfor _, match := range matches {\n126|\t\tif !strings.HasSuffix(match, \"_test.go\") {\n127|\t\t\tproduction = append(production, match)\n128|\t\t}\n129|\t}\n130|\tif len(production) == 0 {\n131|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n132|\t}\n133|\n134|\tvar arms []refusalArm\n135|\tparsed := 0\n136|\tfor _, name := range production {\n137|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n138|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n139|\t\tif err != nil {\n140|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v; an unparseable derivation proves nothing\", name, err)\n141|\t\t}\n142|\t\tparsed++\n143|\t\tcollect := func(functionName string, root ast.Node) {\n144|\t\t\tast.Inspect(root, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n145|\t\t\t\tswitch expression := node.(type) {\n146|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.UnaryExpr:\n147|\t\t\t\t\tif expression.Op != token.AND {\n148|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n149|\t\t\t\t\t}\n150|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.X.(*ast.CompositeLit)\n151|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n152|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n153|\t\t\t\t\t}\n154|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := literal.Type.(*ast.Ident)\n155|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || identifier.Name != \"Error\" {\n156|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n157|\t\t\t\t\t}\n158|\t\t\t\t\tcode, detail := \"\", \"\"\n159|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, element := range literal.Elts {\n160|\t\t\t\t\t\tpair, ok := element.(*ast.KeyValueExpr)\n161|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n162|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n163|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n164|\t\t\t\t\t\tkey, ok := pair.Key.(*ast.Ident)\n165|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n166|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n167|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n168|\t\t\t\t\t\tswitch key.Name {\n169|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Code\":\n170|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsymbol, ok := pair.Value.(*ast.Ident)\n171|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n172|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal code is not a static Code symbol; \"+\n173|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed code cannot be inventoried\", functionName)\n174|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n175|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = symbol.Name\n176|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Detail\":\n177|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdetail = staticDetail(t, functionName, pair.Value)\n178|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n179|\t\t\t\t\t}\n180|\t\t\t\t\tif code == \"\" || detail == \"\" {\n181|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal without a static code and detail; \"+\n182|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"the inventory cannot name what it cannot read\", functionName)\n183|\t\t\t\t\t}\n184|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n185|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n186|\t\t\t\t\t})\n187|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.CallExpr:\n188|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := expression.Fun.(*ast.Ident)\n189|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n190|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n191|\t\t\t\t\t}\n192|\t\t\t\t\tif len(expression.Args) != 1 {\n193|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s with %d arguments; Detail must be a single \"+\n194|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"static literal and never interpolate local data, and a \"+\n195|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"variadic detail cannot be inventoried\",\n196|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName, identifier.Name, len(expression.Args))\n197|\t\t\t\t\t}\n198|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.Args[0].(*ast.BasicLit)\n199|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n200|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s detail is not a static string literal; \"+\n201|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed detail cannot be inventoried\", functionName, identifier.Name)\n202|\t\t\t\t\t}\n203|\t\t\t\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n204|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n205|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: unquote detail: %v\", functionName, err)\n206|\t\t\t\t\t}\n207|\t\t\t\t\tcode := \"CodeMismatch\"\n208|\t\t\t\t\tif identifier.Name == \"integrityFailure\" {\n209|\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = \"CodeIntegrityFailure\"\n210|\t\t\t\t\t}\n211|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n212|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n213|\t\t\t\t\t})\n214|\t\t\t\t}\n215|\t\t\t\treturn true\n216|\t\t\t})\n217|\t\t}\n218|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n219|\t\t\tswitch decl := declaration.(type) {\n220|\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl:\n221|\t\t\t\tif decl.Body == nil {\n222|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n223|\t\t\t\t}\n224|\t\t\t\tif constructorFunctions[decl.Name.Name] {\n225|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n226|\t\t\t\t}\n227|\t\t\t\tfunctionName := decl.Name.Name\n228|\t\t\t\tif decl.Recv != nil && len(decl.Recv.List) > 0 {\n229|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = receiverTypeName(decl.Recv.List[0].Type) + \".\" + functionName\n230|\t\t\t\t}\n231|\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, decl.Body)\n232|\t\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n233|\t\t\t\t// Package-level initializers execute outside any FuncDecl,\n234|\t\t\t\t// so a func literal (or a bare &Error{}) assigned to a\n235|\t\t\t\t// package var would otherwise ship invisible. Attribute\n236|\t\t\t\t// its arms to the declared variable name.\n237|\t\t\t\tfor _, spec := range decl.Specs {\n238|\t\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := spec.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n239|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n240|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n241|\t\t\t\t\t}\n242|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName := \"var\"\n243|\t\t\t\t\tif len(value.Names) > 0 {\n244|\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = value.Names[0].Name\n245|\t\t\t\t\t}\n246|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, item := range value.Values {\n247|\t\t\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, item)\n248|\t\t\t\t\t}\n249|\t\t\t\t}\n250|\t\t\t}\n251|\t\t}\n252|\t\trejectConstructorAliases(t, file, name)\n253|\t}\n254|\t_ = parsed\n255|\tif len(arms) == 0 {\n256|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero refusal arms from the package sources; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n257|\t}\n258|\toccurrences := make(map[refusalArm]int)\n259|\tfor index := range arms {\n260|\t\tkey := arms[index]\n261|\t\tkey.occurrence = 0\n262|\t\toccurrences[key]++\n263|\t\tarms[index].occurrence = occurrences[key]\n264|\t}\n265|\treturn arms\n266|}\n267|\n268|// rejectConstructorAliases fails the suite when a refusal constructor\n269|// (mismatchf, integrityFailure) is referenced outside direct-call\n270|// position. `refuse := mismatchf; refuse(\"…\")` ships a reachable arm the\n271|// arm derivation above cannot attribute to a static call site, so the\n272|// reference itself is the violation: call the constructor directly.\n273|// The constructors' own declarations are excluded; their bodies are the\n274|// funnel, not arms. Any other use — alias, argument, field, shadow —\n275|// fails closed, because no legitimate production shape needs it.\n276|func rejectConstructorAliases(t *testing.T, file *ast.File, name string) {\n277|\tt.Helper()\n278|\n279|\tallowed := map[token.Pos]bool{}\n280|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n281|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n282|\t\tif !ok {\n283|\t\t\tif call, ok := node.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n284|\t\t\t\tif identifier, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.Ident); ok && constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n285|\t\t\t\t\tallowed[identifier.Pos()] = true\n286|\t\t\t\t}\n287|\t\t\t}\n288|\t\t\treturn true\n289|\t\t}\n290|\t\tif constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n291|\t\t\tallowed[declaration.Name.Pos()] = true\n292|\t\t\treturn false\n293|\t\t}\n294|\t\treturn true\n295|\t})\n296|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n297|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n298|\t\tif ok && constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n299|\t\t\treturn false\n300|\t\t}\n301|\t\tidentifier, ok := node.(*ast.Ident)\n302|\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] || allowed[identifier.Pos()] {\n303|\t\t\treturn true\n304|\t\t}\n305|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: constructor %q referenced outside direct-call position; \"+\n306|\t\t\t\"an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, call it directly\", name, identifier.Name)\n307|\t\treturn true\n308|\t})\n309|}\n310|\n311|// receiverTypeName renders a method receiver type to its bare name.\n312|func receiverTypeName(expression ast.Expr) string {\n313|\tswitch typed := expression.(type) {\n314|\tcase *ast.Ident:\n315|\t\treturn typed.Name\n316|\tcase *ast.StarExpr:\n317|\t\treturn receiverTypeName(typed.X)\n318|\tdefault:\n319|\t\treturn \"unknown\"\n320|\t}\n321|}\n322|\n323|// staticDetail reads one Detail expression: a string literal, or the one\n324|// dynamic funnel. Anything else fails the derivation.\n325|func staticDetail(t *testing.T, function string, expression ast.Expr) string {\n326|\tt.Helper()\n327|\n328|\tif literal, ok := expression.(*ast.BasicLit); ok && literal.Kind == token.STRING {\n329|\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n330|\t\tif err != nil {\n331|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: unquote detail: %v\", function, err)\n332|\t\t}\n333|\t\treturn detail\n334|\t}\n335|\tif call, ok := expression.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n336|\t\tif selector, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.SelectorExpr); ok && selector.Sel.Name == \"Error\" {\n337|\t\t\tif receiver, ok := selector.X.(*ast.Ident); ok && receiver.Name == \"err\" {\n338|\t\t\t\treturn passthroughDetail\n339|\t\t\t}\n340|\t\t}\n341|\t}\n342|\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal Detail is not a static clause; Detail must never \"+\n343|\t\t\"interpolate local data, and a dynamic detail cannot be inventoried\", function)\n344|\treturn \"\"\n345|}\n346|\n347|// productionCodeSymbols resolves every Code symbol to its wire value from\n348|// the production const declarations, so the declared table cannot drift\n349|// from the codes production actually emits.\n350|func productionCodeSymbols(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n351|\tt.Helper()\n352|\n353|\tsymbols := make(map[string]string)\n354|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n355|\tif err != nil {\n356|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n357|\t}\n358|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n359|\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n360|\t\t\tcontinue\n361|\t\t}\n362|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n363|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n364|\t\tif err != nil {\n365|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n366|\t\t}\n367|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n368|\t\t\tgeneral, ok := declaration.(*ast.GenDecl)\n369|\t\t\tif !ok || general.Tok != token.CONST {\n370|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n371|\t\t\t}\n372|\t\t\tfor _, specification := range general.Specs {\n373|\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := specification.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n374|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n375|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n376|\t\t\t\t}\n377|\t\t\t\tfor index, name := range value.Names {\n378|\t\t\t\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(name.Name, \"Code\") || index >= len(value.Values) {\n379|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n380|\t\t\t\t\t}\n381|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := value.Values[index].(*ast.BasicLit)\n382|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n383|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"code symbol %s is not a static string; \"+\n384|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"wire codes must be literals\", name.Name)\n385|\t\t\t\t\t}\n386|\t\t\t\t\twire, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n387|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n388|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unquote %s: %v\", name.Name, err)\n389|\t\t\t\t\t}\n390|\t\t\t\t\tsymbols[name.Name] = wire\n391|\t\t\t\t}\n392|\t\t\t}\n393|\t\t}\n394|\t}\n395|\tif len(symbols) == 0 {\n396|\t\tt.Fatal(\"resolved zero code symbols; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n397|\t}\n398|\treturn symbols\n399|}\n400|\n401|// testBodies indexes every test declaration in this package by file and\n402|// name to its body source. A duplicate test name across files fails: row\n403|// references would be ambiguous.\n404|func testBodies(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n405|\tt.Helper()\n406|\n407|\tbodies := make(map[string]string)\n408|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*_test.go\")\n409|\tif err != nil {\n410|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob test files: %v\", err)\n411|\t}\n412|\tif len(matches) == 0 {\n413|\t\tt.Fatal(\"found zero test files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n414|\t}\n415|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n416|\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(name)\n417|\t\tif err != nil {\n418|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read %s: %v\", name, err)\n419|\t\t}\n420|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n421|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n422|\t\tif err != nil {\n423|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n424|\t\t}\n425|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n426|\t\t\tfunction, ok := declaration.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n427|\t\t\tif !ok || !strings.HasPrefix(function.Name.Name, \"Test\") {\n428|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n429|\t\t\t}\n430|\t\t\tstart := fileSet.Position(function.Body.Pos()).Offset\n431|\t\t\tend := fileSet.Position(function.Body.End()).Offset\n432|\t\t\tkey := name + \"\\n\" + function.Name.Name\n433|\t\t\tif _, duplicate := bodies[key]; duplicate {\n434|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"test %s is declared twice; row references would be ambiguous\", key)\n435|\t\t\t}\n436|\t\t\tbodies[key] = string(raw[start:end])\n437|\t\t}\n438|\t}\n439|\tif len(bodies) == 0 {\n440|\t\tt.Fatal(\"indexed zero test declarations, so every row below would resolve vacuously\")\n441|\t}\n442|\treturn bodies\n443|}\n444|\n445|// predicateCodes resolves every Is predicate to the code symbol it\n446|// reports, verifying the shape: a single return of errorCode(err, Code).\n447|// A predicate in any other shape fails: the inventory leans on these to\n448|// resolve code-only assertions, so an unrecognized shape proves nothing.\n449|func predicateCodes(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n450|\tt.Helper()\n451|\n452|\tpredicates := make(map[string]string)\n453|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n454|\tif err != nil {\n455|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n456|\t}\n457|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n458|\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n459|\t\t\tcontinue\n460|\t\t}\n461|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n462|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n463|\t\tif err != nil {\n464|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n465|\t\t}\n466|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n467|\t\t\tfunction, ok := declaration.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n468|\t\t\tif !ok || !strings.HasPrefix(function.Name.Name, \"Is\") || function.Body == nil {\n469|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n470|\t\t\t}\n471|\t\t\tif len(function.Body.List) != 1 {\n472|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s is not a single return; the inventory cannot resolve it\",\n473|\t\t\t\t\tfunction.Name.Name)\n474|\t\t\t}\n475|\t\t\treturned, ok := function.Body.List[0].(*ast.ReturnStmt)\n476|\t\t\tif !ok || len(returned.Results) != 1 {\n477|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s is not a single return; the inventory cannot resolve it\",\n478|\t\t\t\t\tfunction.Name.Name)\n479|\t\t\t}\n480|\t\t\tcall, ok := returned.Results[0].(*ast.CallExpr)\n481|\t\t\tif !ok || len(call.Args) != 2 {\n482|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s does not call errorCode(err, Code); \"+\n483|\t\t\t\t\t\"the inventory cannot resolve it\", function.Name.Name)\n484|\t\t\t}\n485|\t\t\tcode, ok := call.Args[1].(*ast.Ident)\n486|\t\t\tif !ok {\n487|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s reports a non-static code; the inventory cannot resolve it\",\n488|\t\t\t\t\tfunction.Name.Name)\n489|\t\t\t}\n490|\t\t\tpredicates[function.Name.Name] = code.Name\n491|\t\t}\n492|\t}\n493|\tif len(predicates) == 0 {\n494|\t\tt.Fatal(\"resolved zero predicates; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n495|\t}\n496|\treturn predicates\n497|}\n498|\n499|// refusalTestRef names one asserting test by file and declaration name.\n500|type refusalTestRef struct {\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c537","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0798e-8ce3-71d2-82cf-4115ffc6a2dc"},"sequence":246,"recorded_at":1780531400000487,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a27566c0-e07d-4374-b9c6-044054a3f322"},"task_id":"a27566c0-e07d-4374-b9c6-044054a3f322","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"a27566c0-e07d-4374-b9c6-044054a3f322"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c539","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0798e-8ce3-71d2-82cf-4115ffc6a2dc"},"sequence":247,"recorded_at":1780531400000489,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"9185f425-4c66-4496-abcf-30b967c4d7b3"},"task_id":"9185f425-4c66-4496-abcf-30b967c4d7b3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"9185f425-4c66-4496-abcf-30b967c4d7b3","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/digit_guard_census_test.go`.\n1|// Derived digit-guard census over the provider-protocol leaf.\n2|//\n3|// The failure this file exists to prevent: a digit-parsing gate added,\n4|// narrowed, or widened anywhere in this leaf while the suite stays\n5|// green. It happened four rounds in a row — a saturation guard\n6|// witnessed far from its own edge, an exponent bound witnessed 44\n7|// bytes above its true edge, an uncensused semverMajor, and finally a\n8|// pre-multiply guard (`value > 100` in descriptorGeometry) whose\n9|// narrowing to its own arithmetic edge (`value > 922337203685477580`)\n10|// admitted a 37-digit literal as 1 while every shipped vector still\n11|// refused. Each round closed one site with one hand-written row while\n12|// the census listed its own sites, so the next site was invisible by\n13|// construction.\n14|//\n15|// This census derives its denominator from production instead of\n16|// listing it: it parses every production file of internal/\n17|// terminalbackend and internal/provhost (directory-derived, so a new\n18|// file is scanned without anyone remembering it) and enumerates both\n19|// digit-guard shapes in one pass:\n20|//\n21|//   - char: an ordering comparison against a decimal digit rune\n22|//     (`c < '0' || c > '9'` and its spellings, refuse-form or\n23|//     accept-form, including the digit case of a hex decoder);\n24|//   - bound: an ordering comparison against a decimal accumulator —\n25|//     an identifier the same function accumulates through `* 10`\n26|//     (`value > N` / `major > N`, before or after the multiply).\n27|//\n28|// Every derived site carries exactly one declared row: a char row\n29|// names its reachable rejected class, a bound row names its\n30|// arithmetic-edge threshold and its witness. The census fails closed\n31|// in three directions: a derived site with no row, a row with no\n32|// derived site, and a site the classifier cannot place (an equality\n33|// against a digit rune, a chain mixing digit and accumulator\n34|// comparisons, a chain mixing either with unrelated comparisons, or\n35|// a comparison with accumulators on both sides). A zero-file scan, a\n36|// zero-site derivation, an unparseable file, a row with an empty\n37|// claim, and a row naming a test that does not exist are fatal too.\n38|//\n39|// The derivation keys on structure, never on identifier names: rune\n40|// literals and `* 10` accumulations survive renaming, var bindings,\n41|// and import aliases. Control plants prove it (see the battery\n42|// record): a fourth digit gate through a var binding and one through\n43|// an import-aliased file both fail as unregistered sites.\n44|//\n45|// Stated bounds (not inferred):\n46|//   - Non-digit rune guards (`== '.'`, `!= '\\\\'`, `!= 'u'`, the\n47|//     `0xed`/`0xa0` byte ranges) are a different class and invisible\n48|//     to this enumerator. A digit-rune novelty (`== '0'`, `!= '9'`)\n49|//     is derived and fails as unclassifiable.\n50|//   - The hex letter cases (`>= 'a'`, `<= 'F'`) carry no digit rune\n51|//     and are invisible; only the digit case of each hex decoder is\n52|//     rowed. The decoder's exactness across all three cases rests\n53|//     with the canonical-JSON agreement sweeps the hex rows name.\n54|//   - An accumulator with no guard has no bound to row: a missing\n55|//     guard is caught by the overflow-vector tests, not here.\n56|//   - Shadowing an accumulator name inside its own function would\n57|//     misattribute the comparison; no such shadowing exists today.\n58|package terminalbackend_test\n59|\n60|import (\n61|\t\"bytes\"\n62|\t\"go/ast\"\n63|\t\"go/parser\"\n64|\t\"go/printer\"\n65|\t\"go/token\"\n66|\t\"os\"\n67|\t\"path/filepath\"\n68|\t\"sort\"\n69|\t\"strconv\"\n70|\t\"strings\"\n71|\t\"testing\"\n72|\n73|\tterminalbackend \"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n74|)\n75|\n76|// digitGuardSite is one derived production guard: a maximal ||/&&\n77|// chain of comparisons (or one lone comparison) mentioning a digit\n78|// rune or a decimal accumulator, keyed by package directory, file,\n79|// enclosing function, shape, and printer-normalized expression. Two\n80|// identical guards in one function share a key and fail the census\n81|// until they are disambiguated: hiding behind a sibling row is a\n82|// silent admit.\n83|type digitGuardSite struct {\n84|\tdir      string\n85|\tfunction string\n86|\tfile     string\n87|\tkind     string\n88|\texpr     string\n89|}\n90|\n91|// digitGuardRow is the declared counterpart of one site. A char row\n92|// states the reachable rejected class; a bound row states the\n93|// arithmetic-edge threshold and the witness literal that pins it.\n94|// Tests names the driving tests, which must exist.\n95|type digitGuardRow struct {\n96|\tdir       string\n97|\tfile      string\n98|\tfunction  string\n99|\tkind      string\n100|\texpr      string\n101|\trejected  string\n102|\tthreshold string\n103|\twitness   string\n104|\ttests     []string\n105|}\n106|\n107|// digitGuardRows declares every digit guard in the leaf. The expr\n108|// column is the printer-normalized chain text the derivation\n109|// computes; it is exact on purpose, so editing a bound orphans its\n110|// row instead of passing silently.\n111|var digitGuardRows = []digitGuardRow{\n112|\t{\n113|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"descriptor.go\", function: \"descriptorGeometry\",\n114|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `digit < '0' || digit > '9'`,\n115|\t\trejected: \"reachable {-, +, ., e, E}: json.Number literals spell only [0-9.+eE-], so / (0x2F) and : (0x3A) die in the strict decoder before the gate runs (pinned by TestDigitCensusAdjacentsNeverReachGeometryGate); + is equivalent by reachability, legal only after e/E which refuse first\",\n116|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestParseProviderDescriptorValueRefusals\", \"TestDigitCensusAdjacentsNeverReachGeometryGate\"},\n117|\t},\n118|\t{\n119|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"manifest.go\", function: \"readUTF16EscapeUnit\",\n120|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `digit >= '0' && digit <= '9'`,\n121|\t\trejected: \"the digit case of the three-case hex decoder: bytes outside 0-9a-fA-F reach the refuse arm (return false, refused as a document syntax/surrogate escape); the case admits exactly 0-9\",\n122|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestDocumentSurrogateEscapeRefused\", \"TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON\", \"TestDocumentHexEscapeDigitBoundaryRefused\"},\n123|\t},\n124|\t{\n125|\t\tdir: \"provhost\", file: \"protocol.go\", function: \"parseMajor\",\n126|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `digit < '0' || digit > '9'`,\n127|\t\trejected: \"every non-digit byte in the major component (JSON string domain, so any byte is reachable): adjacents / and : witnessed in major position\",\n128|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry\"},\n129|\t},\n130|\t{\n131|\t\tdir: \"provhost\", file: \"protocol.go\", function: \"parseMajor\",\n132|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `rest[i] < '0' || rest[i] > '9'`,\n133|\t\trejected: \"every non-digit byte in each rest component: adjacents / and : witnessed in both minor and patch positions\",\n134|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry\"},\n135|\t},\n136|\t{\n137|\t\tdir: \"provhost\", file: \"surrogate.go\", function: \"readHexUnit\",\n138|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `b >= '0' && b <= '9'`,\n139|\t\trejected: \"the digit branch of the hex if-chain: bytes outside 0-9a-fA-F reach the refuse arm (return false, refused as a lone surrogate escape); the branch admits exactly 0-9\",\n140|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestProductionEntriesRefuseLoneSurrogateEscapes\", \"TestSurrogateGateDerivedSweepAgreesWithCanonicalJSON\", \"TestProductionEntriesRefuseHexDigitBoundaryEscapes\"},\n141|\t},\n142|\t{\n143|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"descriptor.go\", function: \"descriptorGeometry\",\n144|\t\tkind: \"bound\", expr: `value > 100`,\n145|\t\tthreshold: \"100: refuse on the first digit past the bound, before the multiply; value is at most 100 here so value*10+9 cannot wrap on any platform\",\n146|\t\twitness:   \"9223372036854775808000000000000000001 (37 digits): admitted as 1 when the guard narrows to floor(MaxInt/10) = 922337203685477580, refused by every threshold at or below 92233720368547758\",\n147|\t\ttests:     []string{\"TestParseProviderDescriptorGeometryOverflowVectors\"},\n148|\t},\n149|\t{\n150|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"descriptor.go\", function: \"descriptorGeometry\",\n151|\t\tkind: \"bound\", expr: `value < 1 || value > 1000`,\n152|\t\tthreshold: \"lower 1 / upper 1000: the post-accumulation range deciding the 1..1000 bound after the loop\",\n153|\t\twitness:   \"boundary pair 0/1 and 1000/1001, plus 65535\",\n154|\t\ttests:     []string{\"TestParseProviderDescriptorValueRefusals\", \"TestParseProviderDescriptorGeometryBounds\"},\n155|\t},\n156|\t{\n157|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"semverMajor\",\n158|\t\tkind: \"bound\", expr: `major > (math.MaxInt-digit)/10`,\n159|\t\tthreshold: \"floor((MaxInt-digit)/10): saturate to MaxInt, never wrap; largest admitted 9223372036854775807, MaxInt+1 saturates\",\n160|\t\twitness:   \"922337203685477580801.0.0 with neighbours 800/802: walks the accumulator to MaxInt/10 and aliases native major 1 when the guard narrows to MaxInt/10\",\n161|\t\ttests:     []string{\"TestSemverMajorSaturationEdge\"},\n162|\t},\n163|\t{\n164|\t\tdir: \"provhost\", file: \"protocol.go\", function: \"parseMajor\",\n165|\t\tkind: \"bound\", expr: `major > (math.MaxInt-step)/10`,\n166|\t\tthreshold: \"floor((MaxInt-step)/10): saturate to MaxInt, never wrap; largest admitted 9223372036854775807, MaxInt+1 saturates\",\n167|\t\twitness:   \"922337203685477580802.0.0 with neighbours 801/803: walks the accumulator to MaxInt/10 and aliases native major 2 when the guard narrows to MaxInt/10\",\n168|\t\ttests:     []string{\"TestParseMajorSaturationEdge\", \"TestParseMajorNeverWraps\"},\n169|\t},\n170|}\n171|\n172|// digitGuardKey identifies one site or row in both directions.\n173|func digitGuardKey(dir, file, function, kind, expr string) string {\n174|\treturn dir + \"|\" + file + \"|\" + function + \"|\" + kind + \"|\" + expr\n175|}\n176|\n177|// TestDigitCensusCoversEveryLeafGuard derives every digit guard from\n178|// leaf production source and requires each to resolve to exactly one\n179|// declared row naming a real test, and every declared row to resolve\n180|// to exactly one derived guard.\n181|func TestDigitCensusCoversEveryLeafGuard(t *testing.T) {\n182|\tt.Parallel()\n183|\n184|\tsites, unclassifiable, files := deriveDigitGuardSites(t)\n185|\tif len(unclassifiable) > 0 {\n186|\t\tsort.Strings(unclassifiable)\n187|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unclassifiable digit-guard shapes (%d), classify them before the suite passes:\\n%s\",\n188|\t\t\tlen(unclassifiable), strings.Join(unclassifiable, \"\\n\"))\n189|\t}\n190|\tseen := map[string]int{}\n191|\tfor _, site := range sites {\n192|\t\tseen[digitGuardKey(site.dir, site.file, site.function, site.kind, site.expr)]++\n193|\t}\n194|\tfor key, count := range seen {\n195|\t\tif count > 1 {\n196|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived digit guard %q occurs %d times; disambiguate the rows instead of hiding behind a sibling\", key, count)\n197|\t\t}\n198|\t}\n199|\tbyKey := map[string]digitGuardSite{}\n200|\tfor _, site := range sites {\n201|\t\tbyKey[digitGuardKey(site.dir, site.file, site.function, site.kind, site.expr)] = site\n202|\t}\n203|\ttests := digitCensusTestNames(t)\n204|\tvar unregistered []string\n205|\tfor _, site := range sites {\n206|\t\tkey := digitGuardKey(site.dir, site.file, site.function, site.kind, site.expr)\n207|\t\tfound := false\n208|\t\tfor _, row := range digitGuardRows {\n209|\t\t\tif digitGuardKey(row.dir, row.file, row.function, row.kind, row.expr) == key {\n210|\t\t\t\tfound = true\n211|\t\t\t\tbreak\n212|\t\t\t}\n213|\t\t}\n214|\t\tif !found {\n215|\t\t\tunregistered = append(unregistered, \"unregistered \"+site.kind+\" site \"+key)\n216|\t\t}\n217|\t}\n218|\tvar orphan []string\n219|\tfor _, row := range digitGuardRows {\n220|\t\tkey := digitGuardKey(row.dir, row.file, row.function, row.kind, row.expr)\n221|\t\tif _, ok := byKey[key]; !ok {\n222|\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"orphan row \"+key)\n223|\t\t\tcontinue\n224|\t\t}\n225|\t\tswitch row.kind {\n226|\t\tcase \"char\":\n227|\t\t\tif row.rejected == \"\" {\n228|\t\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"char row \"+key+\" declares no rejected class\")\n229|\t\t\t}\n230|\t\t\tif row.threshold != \"\" || row.witness != \"\" {\n231|\t\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"char row \"+key+\" carries bound fields\")\n232|\t\t\t}\n233|\t\tcase \"bound\":\n234|\t\t\tif row.threshold == \"\" || row.witness == \"\" {\n235|\t\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"bound row \"+key+\" declares no threshold or witness\")\n236|\t\t\t}\n237|\t\t\tif row.rejected != \"\" {\n238|\t\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"bound row \"+key+\" carries a rejected class\")\n239|\t\t\t}\n240|\t\tdefault:\n241|\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"row \"+key+\" has unknown kind \"+row.kind)\n242|\t\t}\n243|\t\tif len(row.tests) == 0 {\n244|\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"row \"+key+\" names no driving test\")\n245|\t\t}\n246|\t\tfor _, name := range row.tests {\n247|\t\t\tif !tests[name] {\n248|\t\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"row \"+key+\" names missing test \"+name)\n249|\t\t\t}\n250|\t\t}\n251|\t}\n252|\tif len(unregistered) > 0 || len(orphan) > 0 {\n253|\t\tsort.Strings(unregistered)\n254|\t\tsort.Strings(orphan)\n255|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"digit-guard census mismatch:\\n%s\\n%s\",\n256|\t\t\tstrings.Join(unregistered, \"\\n\"), strings.Join(orphan, \"\\n\"))\n257|\t}\n258|\tt.Logf(\"digit-guard census: %d/%d derived sites rowed across %d production files\",\n259|\t\tlen(sites), len(digitGuardRows), files)\n260|}\n261|\n262|// TestDigitCensusAdjacentsNeverReachGeometryGate proves `/` (0x2F) and\n263|// `:` (0x3A) — the characters adjacent to the digit range — never reach\n264|// the descriptorGeometry gate: neither spells inside a JSON number, so\n265|// the strict decoder refuses first with the document syntax arm. A gate\n266|// mutant shifting either bound (`digit > ':'`, `digit < '/'`) or\n267|// skipping either character token-preservingly changes no disposition\n268|// here; the rows exist so the census claim \"unreachable\" is measured,\n269|// not asserted. Both members are driven because the geometry site is\n270|// shared and the decoder runs before either call.\n271|func TestDigitCensusAdjacentsNeverReachGeometryGate(t *testing.T) {\n272|\tt.Parallel()\n273|\n274|\tfor _, member := range []string{\"columns\", \"rows\"} {\n275|\t\tfor _, literal := range []string{`1/2`, `1:2`} {\n276|\t\t\t_, err := terminalbackend.ParseProviderDescriptor(setDescriptorMember(t, member, literal))\n277|\t\t\tif err == nil || !terminalbackend.IsMismatch(err) {\n278|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ParseProviderDescriptor(%s=%s) error = %v, want a document mismatch refusal\", member, literal, err)\n279|\t\t\t}\n280|\t\t\tif got := refusalDetail(t, err); got != \"document syntax\" {\n281|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ParseProviderDescriptor(%s=%s) detail = %q, want document syntax\", member, literal, got)\n282|\t\t\t}\n283|\t\t}\n284|\t}\n285|}\n286|\n287|// deriveDigitGuardSites parses every production file of the two leaf\n288|// packages and returns every digit-guard site in source order, every\n289|// unclassifiable shape, and the scanned file count. The file set is\n290|// directory-derived: a new production file is scanned without anyone\n291|// remembering it.\n292|func deriveDigitGuardSites(t *testing.T) (sites []digitGuardSite, unclassifiable []string, files int) {\n293|\tt.Helper()\n294|\n295|\troot, err := os.Getwd()\n296|\tif err != nil {\n297|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive digit guards: %v\", err)\n298|\t}\n299|\tdirs := []struct {\n300|\t\tlabel string\n301|\t\tpath  string\n302|\t}{\n303|\t\t{\"terminalbackend\", root},\n304|\t\t{\"provhost\", filepath.Join(root, \"..\", \"provhost\")},\n305|\t}\n306|\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n307|\tfor _, dir := range dirs {\n308|\t\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(dir.path)\n309|\t\tif err != nil {\n310|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive digit guards: read %s: %v\", dir.path, err)\n311|\t\t}\n312|\t\tnames := []string{}\n313|\t\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n314|\t\t\tname := entry.Name()\n315|\t\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(name, \".go\") || strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n316|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n317|\t\t\t}\n318|\t\t\tnames = append(names, name)\n319|\t\t}\n320|\t\tsort.Strings(names)\n321|\t\tfor _, name := range names {\n322|\t\t\tpath := filepath.Join(dir.path, name)\n323|\t\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n324|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n325|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive digit guards: read %s: %v\", path, err)\n326|\t\t\t}\n327|\t\t\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, path, source, 0)\n328|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n329|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive digit guards: parse %s: %v\", path, err)\n330|\t\t\t}\n331|\t\t\tfiles++\n332|\t\t\tfor _, decl := range syntax.Decls {\n333|\t\t\t\tswitch decl := decl.(type) {\n334|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl:\n335|\t\t\t\t\tif decl.Body == nil {\n336|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n337|\t\t\t\t\t}\n338|\t\t\t\t\tfunction := decl.Name.Name\n339|\t\t\t\t\tif decl.Recv != nil && len(decl.Recv.List) > 0 {\n340|\t\t\t\t\t\tfunction = digitGuardReceiver(decl.Recv.List[0].Type) + \".\" + function\n341|\t\t\t\t\t}\n342|\t\t\t\t\tmore, bad := digitGuardSitesInBody(dir.label, name, function, decl.Body)\n343|\t\t\t\t\tsites = append(sites, more...)\n344|\t\t\t\t\tunclassifiable = append(unclassifiable, bad...)\n345|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n346|\t\t\t\t\tmore, bad := digitGuardSitesInInit(dir.label, name, decl)\n347|\t\t\t\t\tsites = append(sites, more...)\n348|\t\t\t\t\tunclassifiable = append(unclassifiable, bad...)\n349|\t\t\t\t}\n350|\t\t\t}\n351|\t\t}\n352|\t}\n353|\tif files == 0 {\n354|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived digit guards from zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the leaf\")\n355|\t}\n356|\tif len(sites) == 0 {\n357|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero digit guards from the leaf sources; the scanner is broken, not the leaf\")\n358|\t}\n359|\treturn sites, unclassifiable, files\n360|}\n361|\n362|// digitGuardReceiver names the receiver type of a method for the site\n363|// key: value and pointer receivers share the key space.\n364|func digitGuardReceiver(expr ast.Expr) string {\n365|\texpr = digitGuardUnparen(expr)\n366|\tif star, ok := expr.(*ast.StarExpr); ok {\n367|\t\treturn digitGuardReceiver(star.X)\n368|\t}\n369|\tif ident, ok := expr.(*ast.Ident); ok {\n370|\t\treturn ident.Name\n371|\t}\n372|\treturn \"recv\"\n373|}\n374|\n375|// digitGuardUnparen strips parentheses.\n376|func digitGuardUnparen(expr ast.Expr) ast.Expr {\n377|\tfor {\n378|\t\tparen, ok := expr.(*ast.ParenExpr)\n379|\t\tif !ok {\n380|\t\t\treturn expr\n381|\t\t}\n382|\t\texpr = paren.X\n383|\t}\n384|}\n385|\n386|// digitGuardSitesInInit scans one package-level declaration with no\n387|// accumulator in scope: only char chains can appear here, and any\n388|// accumulator-shaped comparison fails as unclassifiable rather than\n389|// entering silently.\n390|func digitGuardSitesInInit(dir, file string, decl *ast.GenDecl) ([]digitGuardSite, []string) {\n391|\tvar sites []digitGuardSite\n392|\tvar bad []string\n393|\tast.Inspect(decl, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n394|\t\texpr, ok := node.(ast.Expr)\n395|\t\tif !ok {\n396|\t\t\treturn true\n397|\t\t}\n398|\t\tsite, failure, done := digitGuardClassifyRoot(dir, file, \"(package initializer)\", expr, map[string]bool{})\n399|\t\tif done {\n400|\t\t\tif failure != \"\" {\n401|\t\t\t\tbad = append(bad, failure)\n402|\t\t\t} else if site != nil {\n403|\t\t\t\tsites = append(sites, *site)\n404|\t\t\t}\n405|\t\t\treturn false\n406|\t\t}\n407|\t\treturn true\n408|\t})\n409|\treturn sites, bad\n410|}\n411|\n412|// digitGuardSitesInBody scans one function body. Accumulators are\n413|// collected first so a guard comparison resolves against the\n414|// function's own accumulation steps, never against a name list.\n415|func digitGuardSitesInBody(dir, file, function string, body *ast.BlockStmt) ([]digitGuardSite, []string) {\n416|\taccumulators := digitGuardAccumulators(body)\n417|\tvar sites []digitGuardSite\n418|\tvar bad []string\n419|\tast.Inspect(body, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n420|\t\texpr, ok := node.(ast.Expr)\n421|\t\tif !ok {\n422|\t\t\treturn true\n423|\t\t}\n424|\t\tsite, failure, done := digitGuardClassifyRoot(dir, file, function, expr, accumulators)\n425|\t\tif done {\n426|\t\t\tif failure != \"\" {\n427|\t\t\t\tbad = append(bad, failure)\n428|\t\t\t} else if site != nil {\n429|\t\t\t\tsites = append(sites, *site)\n430|\t\t\t}\n431|\t\t\treturn false\n432|\t\t}\n433|\t\treturn true\n434|\t})\n435|\treturn sites, bad\n436|}\n437|\n438|// digitGuardClassifyRoot decides whether expr is a chain root worth\n439|// classifying: a ||/&& whose parent the Inspect walk already consumed\n440|// is part of the outer chain, and a comparison inside any ||/&&\n441|// chain belongs to its root. Non-root nodes report done=false so the\n442|// walk descends. A root with no digit or accumulator content reports\n443|// done=true with no site, pruning the walk below it.\n444|func digitGuardClassifyRoot(dir, file, function string, expr ast.Expr, accumulators map[string]bool) (*digitGuardSite, string, bool) {\n445|\tbinary, ok := expr.(*ast.BinaryExpr)\n446|\tif !ok {\n447|\t\treturn nil, \"\", false\n448|\t}\n449|\tif binary.Op == token.LOR || binary.Op == token.LAND {\n450|\t\treturn digitGuardClassifyChain(dir, file, function, binary, accumulators)\n451|\t}\n452|\tif digitGuardIsComparison(binary.Op) {\n453|\t\tleaf := digitGuardClassifyLeaf(binary, accumulators)\n454|\t\tswitch leaf {\n455|\t\tcase digitLeafChar:\n456|\t\t\treturn &digitGuardSite{dir: dir, file: file, function: function, kind: \"char\", expr: digitGuardCanon(binary)}, \"\", true\n457|\t\tcase digitLeafBound:\n458|\t\t\treturn &digitGuardSite{dir: dir, file: file, function: function, kind: \"bound\", expr: digitGuardCanon(binary)}, \"\", true\n459|\t\tcase digitLeafBad:\n460|\t\t\treturn nil, \"unclassifiable guard in \" + file + \" (\" + function + \"): \" + digitGuardCanon(binary), true\n461|\t\tdefault:\n462|\t\t\treturn nil, \"\", false\n463|\t\t}\n464|\t}\n465|\treturn nil, \"\", false\n466|}\n467|\n468|// digitGuardClassifyChain gathers the leaves of one maximal ||/&&\n469|// chain and places the chain: pure digit chains are char sites,\n470|// pure accumulator chains are bound sites, anything mixed or\n471|// degenerate is unclassifiable, and chains with no digit or\n472|// accumulator content are pruned.\n473|func digitGuardClassifyChain(dir, file, function string, root *ast.BinaryExpr, accumulators map[string]bool) (*digitGuardSite, string, bool) {\n474|\tvar chars, bounds, other, bad int\n475|\tvar visit func(expr ast.Expr)\n476|\tvisit = func(expr ast.Expr) {\n477|\t\texpr = digitGuardUnparen(expr)\n478|\t\tif inner, ok := expr.(*ast.BinaryExpr); ok && (inner.Op == token.LOR || inner.Op == token.LAND) {\n479|\t\t\tvisit(inner.X)\n480|\t\t\tvisit(inner.Y)\n481|\t\t\treturn\n482|\t\t}\n483|\t\tif negated, ok := expr.(*ast.UnaryExpr); ok && negated.Op == token.NOT {\n484|\t\t\tif digitGuardMentionsDigitOrAccumulator(negated.X, accumulators) {\n485|\t\t\t\tbad++\n486|\t\t\t} else {\n487|\t\t\t\tother++\n488|\t\t\t}\n489|\t\t\treturn\n490|\t\t}\n491|\t\tif comparison, ok := expr.(*ast.BinaryExpr); ok && digitGuardIsComparison(comparison.Op) {\n492|\t\t\tswitch digitGuardClassifyLeaf(comparison, accumulators) {\n493|\t\t\tcase digitLeafChar:\n494|\t\t\t\tchars++\n495|\t\t\tcase digitLeafBound:\n496|\t\t\t\tbounds++\n497|\t\t\tcase digitLeafBad:\n498|\t\t\t\tbad++\n499|\t\t\tdefault:\n500|\t\t\t\tother++\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c53b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0798e-8ce3-71d2-82cf-4115ffc6a2dc"},"sequence":248,"recorded_at":1780531400000491,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"9185f425-4c66-4496-abcf-30b967c4d7b3"},"task_id":"9185f425-4c66-4496-abcf-30b967c4d7b3","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"9185f425-4c66-4496-abcf-30b967c4d7b3"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c53d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0798e-8ce3-71d2-82cf-4115ffc6a2dc"},"sequence":249,"recorded_at":1780531400000493,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a"},"call_id":"call_01a0798f13347bd387f309b44ce83919","text":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`.\n1|// AST-derived refusal-arm inventory for the terminal backend packages.\n2|//\n3|// The failure this file exists to prevent: a brand-new production refusal\n4|// arm carrying a brand-new unasserted detail shipped while `gofmt`,\n5|// `go vet`, `go test ./...`, and `tracecheck` all stayed green. A\n6|// hand-maintained arm list cannot catch that; a derived one can, but only\n7|// if it is checked in BOTH directions. The forward direction alone passes\n8|// vacuously on a truncated derivation: every derived arm asserted is true\n9|// when the derivation silently dropped half the package. So this file\n10|// derives every refusal arm from the production AST, requires each to\n11|// resolve to exactly one declared row naming a real asserting test, and\n12|// requires every declared row to resolve to exactly one derived arm.\n13|//\n14|// Modelled on internal/canonicaljson/grammar_inventory_test.go: derivation\n15|// fails closed on an empty, short, or unparseable input, and the declared\n16|// table cannot move its own goalposts because the derivation never\n17|// consults it.\n18|//\n19|// Stated bounds (not inferred):\n20|//   - The inventory proves every arm is DECLARED with a resolving test.\n21|//     Execution and decision proof is each row's named test, measured by\n22|//     this package's suite. A row resolves textually (detail mention, or\n23|//     entry-plus-code/predicate mention); a wrongly attributed row that\n24|//     still resolves is a review finding, not a green light.\n25|//   - Attribution drift survives through that fallback: a\n26|//     dead-by-construction arm can resolve through a sibling site's test\n27|//     while pointing at the wrong guard. Live example: CheckTransition's\n28|//     \"operation vocabulary\" arm (conformance.go) is unreachable —\n29|//     ParseOperation admits exactly the ten operations transitionTable\n30|//     covers, so lookupTransition never misses — yet the row carries no\n31|//     bound and resolves through TestParseOperationAdmitsOnlyTheTenClosedOperations,\n32|//     which drives ParseOperation's own arm sharing the detail. The five\n33|//     re-parse arms are the contrast: they declare boundDefensiveReparse\n34|//     and TestDefensiveBoundsAreExactlyThese pins the set.\n35|//   - Kill inflation: both inventory directions fail on ANY added or\n36|//     deleted production arm by construction, so an arm-deleting mutant\n37|//     elsewhere reads as killed by the inventory alone with no behavioral\n38|//     change. Mutation scores measured with this file present are NOT\n39|//     comparable to pre-inventory scores; review the failing-test list,\n40|//     not just the exit code.\n41|//   - errors.New/fmt.Errorf sites are not wire refusals and carry no arm.\n42|//     They live only in validatePlatforms (funneled into one *Error arm\n43|//     whose detail set is pinned exactly) and DigestFile (I/O errors that\n44|//     must never be *Error). Both properties are asserted below, in every\n45|//     FuncDecl body plus every package-level var initializer, and any\n46|//     reference to either constructor outside direct-call position\n47|//     (e.g. `newPlain := errors.New`) fails the suite, so an aliased\n48|//     construction cannot ship unattributed.\n49|//   - The DigestFile half of that allowlist is function-wide with no\n50|//     detail pin, unlike validatePlatforms' derived exact set: a new\n51|//     errors.New on any path inside DigestFile passes the gate (and the\n52|//     never-wire behavioral assertion, which only drives the current\n53|//     paths). Disclosed, not closed.\n54|//   - Custom error types outside the two recognised spellings (*Error,\n55|//     errors.New, fmt.Errorf) are outside both derivations: a bespoke\n56|//     error type smuggled as a refusal survives. Disclosed, not closed.\n57|//   - Constructor Details are single static literals by assertion: the\n58|//     derivation fatals on any mismatchf/integrityFailure call without\n59|//     exactly one string-literal argument, so format-verb interpolation\n60|//     cannot enter the table. Zero multi-argument sites today; go vet's\n61|//     printf analyzer independently refuses a non-constant format string.\n62|package terminalbackend\n63|\n64|import (\n65|\t\"errors\"\n66|\t\"go/ast\"\n67|\t\"go/parser\"\n68|\t\"go/token\"\n69|\t\"os\"\n70|\t\"path/filepath\"\n71|\t\"strconv\"\n72|\t\"strings\"\n73|\t\"testing\"\n74|)\n75|\n76|// refusalArm is one derived production refusal: a wire-code *Error\n77|// construction site keyed by file, enclosing function (receiver-qualified\n78|// for methods), code symbol, static detail, and occurrence index within\n79|// that key. The index keeps two identical arms in one function distinct:\n80|// adding a second arm with an already-declared key fails on the missing\n81|// #2 row instead of hiding behind #1.\n82|type refusalArm struct {\n83|\tfile       string\n84|\tfunction   string\n85|\tcode       string\n86|\tdetail     string\n87|\toccurrence int\n88|}\n89|\n90|// constructorFunctions build refusals instead of issuing them. Their own\n91|// *Error sites are the funnel, not arms.\n92|var constructorFunctions = map[string]bool{\n93|\t\"mismatchf\":        true,\n94|\t\"integrityFailure\": true,\n95|}\n96|\n97|// passthroughDetail marks the single dynamic-detail funnel: Registration\n98|// validation wraps validatePlatforms errors via err.Error(). Every other\n99|// Detail expression must be a static string literal; a new dynamic detail\n100|// fails the derivation rather than entering the table silently.\n101|const passthroughDetail = \"passthrough:err.Error()\"\n102|\n103|// deriveRefusalArms walks every production file of this package (every\n104|// *.go except *_test.go, so a new production file is scanned without\n105|// anyone remembering it) and returns every refusal arm in source order.\n106|// It fails closed: an unparseable file, a non-static code or detail, and\n107|// an empty result are all fatal, never an empty table.\n108|//\n109|// Coverage is declaration-complete, not FuncDecl-complete: every FuncDecl\n110|// body (including nested func literals, methods, and init) plus every\n111|// package-level var initializer is scanned, so a refusal arm hiding in a\n112|// package-level `var f = func() *Error {...}` is derived like any other.\n113|// Constructor references outside direct-call position (`refuse :=\n114|// mismatchf`) are rejected outright by rejectConstructorAliases below:\n115|// an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, so it fails the suite rather\n116|// than shipping silently.\n117|func deriveRefusalArms(t *testing.T) []refusalArm {\n118|\tt.Helper()\n119|\n120|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n121|\tif err != nil {\n122|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n123|\t}\n124|\tvar production []string\n125|\tfor _, match := range matches {\n126|\t\tif !strings.HasSuffix(match, \"_test.go\") {\n127|\t\t\tproduction = append(production, match)\n128|\t\t}\n129|\t}\n130|\tif len(production) == 0 {\n131|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n132|\t}\n133|\n134|\tvar arms []refusalArm\n135|\tparsed := 0\n136|\tfor _, name := range production {\n137|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n138|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n139|\t\tif err != nil {\n140|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v; an unparseable derivation proves nothing\", name, err)\n141|\t\t}\n142|\t\tparsed++\n143|\t\tcollect := func(functionName string, root ast.Node) {\n144|\t\t\tast.Inspect(root, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n145|\t\t\t\tswitch expression := node.(type) {\n146|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.UnaryExpr:\n147|\t\t\t\t\tif expression.Op != token.AND {\n148|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n149|\t\t\t\t\t}\n150|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.X.(*ast.CompositeLit)\n151|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n152|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n153|\t\t\t\t\t}\n154|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := literal.Type.(*ast.Ident)\n155|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || identifier.Name != \"Error\" {\n156|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n157|\t\t\t\t\t}\n158|\t\t\t\t\tcode, detail := \"\", \"\"\n159|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, element := range literal.Elts {\n160|\t\t\t\t\t\tpair, ok := element.(*ast.KeyValueExpr)\n161|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n162|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n163|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n164|\t\t\t\t\t\tkey, ok := pair.Key.(*ast.Ident)\n165|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n166|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n167|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n168|\t\t\t\t\t\tswitch key.Name {\n169|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Code\":\n170|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsymbol, ok := pair.Value.(*ast.Ident)\n171|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n172|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal code is not a static Code symbol; \"+\n173|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed code cannot be inventoried\", functionName)\n174|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n175|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = symbol.Name\n176|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Detail\":\n177|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdetail = staticDetail(t, functionName, pair.Value)\n178|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n179|\t\t\t\t\t}\n180|\t\t\t\t\tif code == \"\" || detail == \"\" {\n181|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal without a static code and detail; \"+\n182|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"the inventory cannot name what it cannot read\", functionName)\n183|\t\t\t\t\t}\n184|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n185|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n186|\t\t\t\t\t})\n187|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.CallExpr:\n188|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := expression.Fun.(*ast.Ident)\n189|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n190|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n191|\t\t\t\t\t}\n192|\t\t\t\t\tif len(expression.Args) != 1 {\n193|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s with %d arguments; Detail must be a single \"+\n194|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"static literal and never interpolate local data, and a \"+\n195|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"variadic detail cannot be inventoried\",\n196|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName, identifier.Name, len(expression.Args))\n197|\t\t\t\t\t}\n198|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.Args[0].(*ast.BasicLit)\n199|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n200|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s detail is not a static string literal; \"+\n201|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed detail cannot be inventoried\", functionName, identifier.Name)\n202|\t\t\t\t\t}\n203|\t\t\t\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n204|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n205|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: unquote detail: %v\", functionName, err)\n206|\t\t\t\t\t}\n207|\t\t\t\t\tcode := \"CodeMismatch\"\n208|\t\t\t\t\tif identifier.Name == \"integrityFailure\" {\n209|\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = \"CodeIntegrityFailure\"\n210|\t\t\t\t\t}\n211|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n212|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n213|\t\t\t\t\t})\n214|\t\t\t\t}\n215|\t\t\t\treturn true\n216|\t\t\t})\n217|\t\t}\n218|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n219|\t\t\tswitch decl := declaration.(type) {\n220|\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl:\n221|\t\t\t\tif decl.Body == nil {\n222|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n223|\t\t\t\t}\n224|\t\t\t\tif constructorFunctions[decl.Name.Name] {\n225|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n226|\t\t\t\t}\n227|\t\t\t\tfunctionName := decl.Name.Name\n228|\t\t\t\tif decl.Recv != nil && len(decl.Recv.List) > 0 {\n229|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = receiverTypeName(decl.Recv.List[0].Type) + \".\" + functionName\n230|\t\t\t\t}\n231|\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, decl.Body)\n232|\t\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n233|\t\t\t\t// Package-level initializers execute outside any FuncDecl,\n234|\t\t\t\t// so a func literal (or a bare &Error{}) assigned to a\n235|\t\t\t\t// package var would otherwise ship invisible. Attribute\n236|\t\t\t\t// its arms to the declared variable name.\n237|\t\t\t\tfor _, spec := range decl.Specs {\n238|\t\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := spec.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n239|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n240|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n241|\t\t\t\t\t}\n242|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName := \"var\"\n243|\t\t\t\t\tif len(value.Names) > 0 {\n244|\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = value.Names[0].Name\n245|\t\t\t\t\t}\n246|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, item := range value.Values {\n247|\t\t\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, item)\n248|\t\t\t\t\t}\n249|\t\t\t\t}\n250|\t\t\t}\n251|\t\t}\n252|\t\trejectConstructorAliases(t, file, name)\n253|\t}\n254|\t_ = parsed\n255|\tif len(arms) == 0 {\n256|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero refusal arms from the package sources; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n257|\t}\n258|\toccurrences := make(map[refusalArm]int)\n259|\tfor index := range arms {\n260|\t\tkey := arms[index]\n261|\t\tkey.occurrence = 0\n262|\t\toccurrences[key]++\n263|\t\tarms[index].occurrence = occurrences[key]\n264|\t}\n265|\treturn arms\n266|}\n267|\n268|// rejectConstructorAliases fails the suite when a refusal constructor\n269|// (mismatchf, integrityFailure) is referenced outside direct-call\n270|// position. `refuse := mismatchf; refuse(\"…\")` ships a reachable arm the\n271|// arm derivation above cannot attribute to a static call site, so the\n272|// reference itself is the violation: call the constructor directly.\n273|// The constructors' own declarations are excluded; their bodies are the\n274|// funnel, not arms. Any other use — alias, argument, field, shadow —\n275|// fails closed, because no legitimate production shape needs it.\n276|func rejectConstructorAliases(t *testing.T, file *ast.File, name string) {\n277|\tt.Helper()\n278|\n279|\tallowed := map[token.Pos]bool{}\n280|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n281|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n282|\t\tif !ok {\n283|\t\t\tif call, ok := node.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n284|\t\t\t\tif identifier, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.Ident); ok && constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n285|\t\t\t\t\tallowed[identifier.Pos()] = true\n286|\t\t\t\t}\n287|\t\t\t}\n288|\t\t\treturn true\n289|\t\t}\n290|\t\tif constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n291|\t\t\tallowed[declaration.Name.Pos()] = true\n292|\t\t\treturn false\n293|\t\t}\n294|\t\treturn true\n295|\t})\n296|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n297|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n298|\t\tif ok && constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n299|\t\t\treturn false\n300|\t\t}\n301|\t\tidentifier, ok := node.(*ast.Ident)\n302|\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] || allowed[identifier.Pos()] {\n303|\t\t\treturn true\n304|\t\t}\n305|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: constructor %q referenced outside direct-call position; \"+\n306|\t\t\t\"an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, call it directly\", name, identifier.Name)\n307|\t\treturn true\n308|\t})\n309|}\n310|\n311|// receiverTypeName renders a method receiver type to its bare name.\n312|func receiverTypeName(expression ast.Expr) string {\n313|\tswitch typed := expression.(type) {\n314|\tcase *ast.Ident:\n315|\t\treturn typed.Name\n316|\tcase *ast.StarExpr:\n317|\t\treturn receiverTypeName(typed.X)\n318|\tdefault:\n319|\t\treturn \"unknown\"\n320|\t}\n321|}\n322|\n323|// staticDetail reads one Detail expression: a string literal, or the one\n324|// dynamic funnel. Anything else fails the derivation.\n325|func staticDetail(t *testing.T, function string, expression ast.Expr) string {\n326|\tt.Helper()\n327|\n328|\tif literal, ok := expression.(*ast.BasicLit); ok && literal.Kind == token.STRING {\n329|\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n330|\t\tif err != nil {\n331|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: unquote detail: %v\", function, err)\n332|\t\t}\n333|\t\treturn detail\n334|\t}\n335|\tif call, ok := expression.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n336|\t\tif selector, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.SelectorExpr); ok && selector.Sel.Name == \"Error\" {\n337|\t\t\tif receiver, ok := selector.X.(*ast.Ident); ok && receiver.Name == \"err\" {\n338|\t\t\t\treturn passthroughDetail\n339|\t\t\t}\n340|\t\t}\n341|\t}\n342|\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal Detail is not a static clause; Detail must never \"+\n343|\t\t\"interpolate local data, and a dynamic detail cannot be inventoried\", function)\n344|\treturn \"\"\n345|}\n346|\n347|// productionCodeSymbols resolves every Code symbol to its wire value from\n348|// the production const declarations, so the declared table cannot drift\n349|// from the codes production actually emits.\n350|func productionCodeSymbols(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n351|\tt.Helper()\n352|\n353|\tsymbols := make(map[string]string)\n354|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n355|\tif err != nil {\n356|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n357|\t}\n358|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n359|\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n360|\t\t\tcontinue\n361|\t\t}\n362|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n363|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n364|\t\tif err != nil {\n365|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n366|\t\t}\n367|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n368|\t\t\tgeneral, ok := declaration.(*ast.GenDecl)\n369|\t\t\tif !ok || general.Tok != token.CONST {\n370|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n371|\t\t\t}\n372|\t\t\tfor _, specification := range general.Specs {\n373|\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := specification.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n374|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n375|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n376|\t\t\t\t}\n377|\t\t\t\tfor index, name := range value.Names {\n378|\t\t\t\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(name.Name, \"Code\") || index >= len(value.Values) {\n379|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n380|\t\t\t\t\t}\n381|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := value.Values[index].(*ast.BasicLit)\n382|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n383|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"code symbol %s is not a static string; \"+\n384|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"wire codes must be literals\", name.Name)\n385|\t\t\t\t\t}\n386|\t\t\t\t\twire, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n387|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n388|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unquote %s: %v\", name.Name, err)\n389|\t\t\t\t\t}\n390|\t\t\t\t\tsymbols[name.Name] = wire\n391|\t\t\t\t}\n392|\t\t\t}\n393|\t\t}\n394|\t}\n395|\tif len(symbols) == 0 {\n396|\t\tt.Fatal(\"resolved zero code symbols; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n397|\t}\n398|\treturn symbols\n399|}\n400|\n401|// testBodies indexes every test declaration in this package by file and\n402|// name to its body source. A duplicate test name across files fails: row\n403|// references would be ambiguous.\n404|func testBodies(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n405|\tt.Helper()\n406|\n407|\tbodies := make(map[string]string)\n408|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*_test.go\")\n409|\tif err != nil {\n410|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob test files: %v\", err)\n411|\t}\n412|\tif len(matches) == 0 {\n413|\t\tt.Fatal(\"found zero test files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n414|\t}\n415|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n416|\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(name)\n417|\t\tif err != nil {\n418|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read %s: %v\", name, err)\n419|\t\t}\n420|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n421|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n422|\t\tif err != nil {\n423|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n424|\t\t}\n425|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n426|\t\t\tfunction, ok := declaration.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n427|\t\t\tif !ok || !strings.HasPrefix(function.Name.Name, \"Test\") {\n428|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n429|\t\t\t}\n430|\t\t\tstart := fileSet.Position(function.Body.Pos()).Offset\n431|\t\t\tend := fileSet.Position(function.Body.End()).Offset\n432|\t\t\tkey := name + \"\\n\" + function.Name.Name\n433|\t\t\tif _, duplicate := bodies[key]; duplicate {\n434|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"test %s is declared twice; row references would be ambiguous\", key)\n435|\t\t\t}\n436|\t\t\tbodies[key] = string(raw[start:end])\n437|\t\t}\n438|\t}\n439|\tif len(bodies) == 0 {\n440|\t\tt.Fatal(\"indexed zero test declarations, so every row below would resolve vacuously\")\n441|\t}\n442|\treturn bodies\n443|}\n444|\n445|// predicateCodes resolves every Is predicate to the code symbol it\n446|// reports, verifying the shape: a single return of errorCode(err, Code).\n447|// A predicate in any other shape fails: the inventory leans on these to\n448|// resolve code-only assertions, so an unrecognized shape proves nothing.\n449|func predicateCodes(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n450|\tt.Helper()\n451|\n452|\tpredicates := make(map[string]string)\n453|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n454|\tif err != nil {\n455|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n456|\t}\n457|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n458|\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n459|\t\t\tcontinue\n460|\t\t}\n461|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n462|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n463|\t\tif err != nil {\n464|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n465|\t\t}\n466|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n467|\t\t\tfunction, ok := declaration.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n468|\t\t\tif !ok || !strings.HasPrefix(function.Name.Name, \"Is\") || function.Body == nil {\n469|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n470|\t\t\t}\n471|\t\t\tif len(function.Body.List) != 1 {\n472|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s is not a single return; the inventory cannot resolve it\",\n473|\t\t\t\t\tfunction.Name.Name)\n474|\t\t\t}\n475|\t\t\treturned, ok := function.Body.List[0].(*ast.ReturnStmt)\n476|\t\t\tif !ok || len(returned.Results) != 1 {\n477|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s is not a single return; the inventory cannot resolve it\",\n478|\t\t\t\t\tfunction.Name.Name)\n479|\t\t\t}\n480|\t\t\tcall, ok := returned.Results[0].(*ast.CallExpr)\n481|\t\t\tif !ok || len(call.Args) != 2 {\n482|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s does not call errorCode(err, Code); \"+\n483|\t\t\t\t\t\"the inventory cannot resolve it\", function.Name.Name)\n484|\t\t\t}\n485|\t\t\tcode, ok := call.Args[1].(*ast.Ident)\n486|\t\t\tif !ok {\n487|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"predicate %s reports a non-static code; the inventory cannot resolve it\",\n488|\t\t\t\t\tfunction.Name.Name)\n489|\t\t\t}\n490|\t\t\tpredicates[function.Name.Name] = code.Name\n491|\t\t}\n492|\t}\n493|\tif len(predicates) == 0 {\n494|\t\tt.Fatal(\"resolved zero predicates; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n495|\t}\n496|\treturn predicates\n497|}\n498|\n499|// refusalTestRef names one asserting test by file and declaration name.\n500|type refusalTestRef struct {\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c53f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0798e-8ce3-71d2-82cf-4115ffc6a2dc"},"sequence":250,"recorded_at":1780531400000495,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a"},"call_id":"call_01a0798f14047c13942aec5aaeb096b3","text":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/digit_guard_census_test.go`.\n1|// Derived digit-guard census over the provider-protocol leaf.\n2|//\n3|// The failure this file exists to prevent: a digit-parsing gate added,\n4|// narrowed, or widened anywhere in this leaf while the suite stays\n5|// green. It happened four rounds in a row — a saturation guard\n6|// witnessed far from its own edge, an exponent bound witnessed 44\n7|// bytes above its true edge, an uncensused semverMajor, and finally a\n8|// pre-multiply guard (`value > 100` in descriptorGeometry) whose\n9|// narrowing to its own arithmetic edge (`value > 922337203685477580`)\n10|// admitted a 37-digit literal as 1 while every shipped vector still\n11|// refused. Each round closed one site with one hand-written row while\n12|// the census listed its own sites, so the next site was invisible by\n13|// construction.\n14|//\n15|// This census derives its denominator from production instead of\n16|// listing it: it parses every production file of internal/\n17|// terminalbackend and internal/provhost (directory-derived, so a new\n18|// file is scanned without anyone remembering it) and enumerates both\n19|// digit-guard shapes in one pass:\n20|//\n21|//   - char: an ordering comparison against a decimal digit rune\n22|//     (`c < '0' || c > '9'` and its spellings, refuse-form or\n23|//     accept-form, including the digit case of a hex decoder);\n24|//   - bound: an ordering comparison against a decimal accumulator —\n25|//     an identifier the same function accumulates through `* 10`\n26|//     (`value > N` / `major > N`, before or after the multiply).\n27|//\n28|// Every derived site carries exactly one declared row: a char row\n29|// names its reachable rejected class, a bound row names its\n30|// arithmetic-edge threshold and its witness. The census fails closed\n31|// in three directions: a derived site with no row, a row with no\n32|// derived site, and a site the classifier cannot place (an equality\n33|// against a digit rune, a chain mixing digit and accumulator\n34|// comparisons, a chain mixing either with unrelated comparisons, or\n35|// a comparison with accumulators on both sides). A zero-file scan, a\n36|// zero-site derivation, an unparseable file, a row with an empty\n37|// claim, and a row naming a test that does not exist are fatal too.\n38|//\n39|// The derivation keys on structure, never on identifier names: rune\n40|// literals and `* 10` accumulations survive renaming, var bindings,\n41|// and import aliases. Control plants prove it (see the battery\n42|// record): a fourth digit gate through a var binding and one through\n43|// an import-aliased file both fail as unregistered sites.\n44|//\n45|// Stated bounds (not inferred):\n46|//   - Non-digit rune guards (`== '.'`, `!= '\\\\'`, `!= 'u'`, the\n47|//     `0xed`/`0xa0` byte ranges) are a different class and invisible\n48|//     to this enumerator. A digit-rune novelty (`== '0'`, `!= '9'`)\n49|//     is derived and fails as unclassifiable.\n50|//   - The hex letter cases (`>= 'a'`, `<= 'F'`) carry no digit rune\n51|//     and are invisible; only the digit case of each hex decoder is\n52|//     rowed. The decoder's exactness across all three cases rests\n53|//     with the canonical-JSON agreement sweeps the hex rows name.\n54|//   - An accumulator with no guard has no bound to row: a missing\n55|//     guard is caught by the overflow-vector tests, not here.\n56|//   - Shadowing an accumulator name inside its own function would\n57|//     misattribute the comparison; no such shadowing exists today.\n58|package terminalbackend_test\n59|\n60|import (\n61|\t\"bytes\"\n62|\t\"go/ast\"\n63|\t\"go/parser\"\n64|\t\"go/printer\"\n65|\t\"go/token\"\n66|\t\"os\"\n67|\t\"path/filepath\"\n68|\t\"sort\"\n69|\t\"strconv\"\n70|\t\"strings\"\n71|\t\"testing\"\n72|\n73|\tterminalbackend \"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n74|)\n75|\n76|// digitGuardSite is one derived production guard: a maximal ||/&&\n77|// chain of comparisons (or one lone comparison) mentioning a digit\n78|// rune or a decimal accumulator, keyed by package directory, file,\n79|// enclosing function, shape, and printer-normalized expression. Two\n80|// identical guards in one function share a key and fail the census\n81|// until they are disambiguated: hiding behind a sibling row is a\n82|// silent admit.\n83|type digitGuardSite struct {\n84|\tdir      string\n85|\tfunction string\n86|\tfile     string\n87|\tkind     string\n88|\texpr     string\n89|}\n90|\n91|// digitGuardRow is the declared counterpart of one site. A char row\n92|// states the reachable rejected class; a bound row states the\n93|// arithmetic-edge threshold and the witness literal that pins it.\n94|// Tests names the driving tests, which must exist.\n95|type digitGuardRow struct {\n96|\tdir       string\n97|\tfile      string\n98|\tfunction  string\n99|\tkind      string\n100|\texpr      string\n101|\trejected  string\n102|\tthreshold string\n103|\twitness   string\n104|\ttests     []string\n105|}\n106|\n107|// digitGuardRows declares every digit guard in the leaf. The expr\n108|// column is the printer-normalized chain text the derivation\n109|// computes; it is exact on purpose, so editing a bound orphans its\n110|// row instead of passing silently.\n111|var digitGuardRows = []digitGuardRow{\n112|\t{\n113|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"descriptor.go\", function: \"descriptorGeometry\",\n114|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `digit < '0' || digit > '9'`,\n115|\t\trejected: \"reachable {-, +, ., e, E}: json.Number literals spell only [0-9.+eE-], so / (0x2F) and : (0x3A) die in the strict decoder before the gate runs (pinned by TestDigitCensusAdjacentsNeverReachGeometryGate); + is equivalent by reachability, legal only after e/E which refuse first\",\n116|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestParseProviderDescriptorValueRefusals\", \"TestDigitCensusAdjacentsNeverReachGeometryGate\"},\n117|\t},\n118|\t{\n119|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"manifest.go\", function: \"readUTF16EscapeUnit\",\n120|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `digit >= '0' && digit <= '9'`,\n121|\t\trejected: \"the digit case of the three-case hex decoder: bytes outside 0-9a-fA-F reach the refuse arm (return false, refused as a document syntax/surrogate escape); the case admits exactly 0-9\",\n122|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestDocumentSurrogateEscapeRefused\", \"TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON\", \"TestDocumentHexEscapeDigitBoundaryRefused\"},\n123|\t},\n124|\t{\n125|\t\tdir: \"provhost\", file: \"protocol.go\", function: \"parseMajor\",\n126|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `digit < '0' || digit > '9'`,\n127|\t\trejected: \"every non-digit byte in the major component (JSON string domain, so any byte is reachable): adjacents / and : witnessed in major position\",\n128|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry\"},\n129|\t},\n130|\t{\n131|\t\tdir: \"provhost\", file: \"protocol.go\", function: \"parseMajor\",\n132|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `rest[i] < '0' || rest[i] > '9'`,\n133|\t\trejected: \"every non-digit byte in each rest component: adjacents / and : witnessed in both minor and patch positions\",\n134|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry\"},\n135|\t},\n136|\t{\n137|\t\tdir: \"provhost\", file: \"surrogate.go\", function: \"readHexUnit\",\n138|\t\tkind: \"char\", expr: `b >= '0' && b <= '9'`,\n139|\t\trejected: \"the digit branch of the hex if-chain: bytes outside 0-9a-fA-F reach the refuse arm (return false, refused as a lone surrogate escape); the branch admits exactly 0-9\",\n140|\t\ttests:    []string{\"TestProductionEntriesRefuseLoneSurrogateEscapes\", \"TestSurrogateGateDerivedSweepAgreesWithCanonicalJSON\", \"TestProductionEntriesRefuseHexDigitBoundaryEscapes\"},\n141|\t},\n142|\t{\n143|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"descriptor.go\", function: \"descriptorGeometry\",\n144|\t\tkind: \"bound\", expr: `value > 100`,\n145|\t\tthreshold: \"100: refuse on the first digit past the bound, before the multiply; value is at most 100 here so value*10+9 cannot wrap on any platform\",\n146|\t\twitness:   \"9223372036854775808000000000000000001 (37 digits): admitted as 1 when the guard narrows to floor(MaxInt/10) = 922337203685477580, refused by every threshold at or below 92233720368547758\",\n147|\t\ttests:     []string{\"TestParseProviderDescriptorGeometryOverflowVectors\"},\n148|\t},\n149|\t{\n150|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"descriptor.go\", function: \"descriptorGeometry\",\n151|\t\tkind: \"bound\", expr: `value < 1 || value > 1000`,\n152|\t\tthreshold: \"lower 1 / upper 1000: the post-accumulation range deciding the 1..1000 bound after the loop\",\n153|\t\twitness:   \"boundary pair 0/1 and 1000/1001, plus 65535\",\n154|\t\ttests:     []string{\"TestParseProviderDescriptorValueRefusals\", \"TestParseProviderDescriptorGeometryBounds\"},\n155|\t},\n156|\t{\n157|\t\tdir: \"terminalbackend\", file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"semverMajor\",\n158|\t\tkind: \"bound\", expr: `major > (math.MaxInt-digit)/10`,\n159|\t\tthreshold: \"floor((MaxInt-digit)/10): saturate to MaxInt, never wrap; largest admitted 9223372036854775807, MaxInt+1 saturates\",\n160|\t\twitness:   \"922337203685477580801.0.0 with neighbours 800/802: walks the accumulator to MaxInt/10 and aliases native major 1 when the guard narrows to MaxInt/10\",\n161|\t\ttests:     []string{\"TestSemverMajorSaturationEdge\"},\n162|\t},\n163|\t{\n164|\t\tdir: \"provhost\", file: \"protocol.go\", function: \"parseMajor\",\n165|\t\tkind: \"bound\", expr: `major > (math.MaxInt-step)/10`,\n166|\t\tthreshold: \"floor((MaxInt-step)/10): saturate to MaxInt, never wrap; largest admitted 9223372036854775807, MaxInt+1 saturates\",\n167|\t\twitness:   \"922337203685477580802.0.0 with neighbours 801/803: walks the accumulator to MaxInt/10 and aliases native major 2 when the guard narrows to MaxInt/10\",\n168|\t\ttests:     []string{\"TestParseMajorSaturationEdge\", \"TestParseMajorNeverWraps\"},\n169|\t},\n170|}\n171|\n172|// digitGuardKey identifies one site or row in both directions.\n173|func digitGuardKey(dir, file, function, kind, expr string) string {\n174|\treturn dir + \"|\" + file + \"|\" + function + \"|\" + kind + \"|\" + expr\n175|}\n176|\n177|// TestDigitCensusCoversEveryLeafGuard derives every digit guard from\n178|// leaf production source and requires each to resolve to exactly one\n179|// declared row naming a real test, and every declared row to resolve\n180|// to exactly one derived guard.\n181|func TestDigitCensusCoversEveryLeafGuard(t *testing.T) {\n182|\tt.Parallel()\n183|\n184|\tsites, unclassifiable, files := deriveDigitGuardSites(t)\n185|\tif len(unclassifiable) > 0 {\n186|\t\tsort.Strings(unclassifiable)\n187|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unclassifiable digit-guard shapes (%d), classify them before the suite passes:\\n%s\",\n188|\t\t\tlen(unclassifiable), strings.Join(unclassifiable, \"\\n\"))\n189|\t}\n190|\tseen := map[string]int{}\n191|\tfor _, site := range sites {\n192|\t\tseen[digitGuardKey(site.dir, site.file, site.function, site.kind, site.expr)]++\n193|\t}\n194|\tfor key, count := range seen {\n195|\t\tif count > 1 {\n196|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived digit guard %q occurs %d times; disambiguate the rows instead of hiding behind a sibling\", key, count)\n197|\t\t}\n198|\t}\n199|\tbyKey := map[string]digitGuardSite{}\n200|\tfor _, site := range sites {\n201|\t\tbyKey[digitGuardKey(site.dir, site.file, site.function, site.kind, site.expr)] = site\n202|\t}\n203|\ttests := digitCensusTestNames(t)\n204|\tvar unregistered []string\n205|\tfor _, site := range sites {\n206|\t\tkey := digitGuardKey(site.dir, site.file, site.function, site.kind, site.expr)\n207|\t\tfound := false\n208|\t\tfor _, row := range digitGuardRows {\n209|\t\t\tif digitGuardKey(row.dir, row.file, row.function, row.kind, row.expr) == key {\n210|\t\t\t\tfound = true\n211|\t\t\t\tbreak\n212|\t\t\t}\n213|\t\t}\n214|\t\tif !found {\n215|\t\t\tunregistered = append(unregistered, \"unregistered \"+site.kind+\" site \"+key)\n216|\t\t}\n217|\t}\n218|\tvar orphan []string\n219|\tfor _, row := range digitGuardRows {\n220|\t\tkey := digitGuardKey(row.dir, row.file, row.function, row.kind, row.expr)\n221|\t\tif _, ok := byKey[key]; !ok {\n222|\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"orphan row \"+key)\n223|\t\t\tcontinue\n224|\t\t}\n225|\t\tswitch row.kind {\n226|\t\tcase \"char\":\n227|\t\t\tif row.rejected == \"\" {\n228|\t\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"char row \"+key+\" declares no rejected class\")\n229|\t\t\t}\n230|\t\t\tif row.threshold != \"\" || row.witness != \"\" {\n231|\t\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"char row \"+key+\" carries bound fields\")\n232|\t\t\t}\n233|\t\tcase \"bound\":\n234|\t\t\tif row.threshold == \"\" || row.witness == \"\" {\n235|\t\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"bound row \"+key+\" declares no threshold or witness\")\n236|\t\t\t}\n237|\t\t\tif row.rejected != \"\" {\n238|\t\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"bound row \"+key+\" carries a rejected class\")\n239|\t\t\t}\n240|\t\tdefault:\n241|\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"row \"+key+\" has unknown kind \"+row.kind)\n242|\t\t}\n243|\t\tif len(row.tests) == 0 {\n244|\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"row \"+key+\" names no driving test\")\n245|\t\t}\n246|\t\tfor _, name := range row.tests {\n247|\t\t\tif !tests[name] {\n248|\t\t\t\torphan = append(orphan, \"row \"+key+\" names missing test \"+name)\n249|\t\t\t}\n250|\t\t}\n251|\t}\n252|\tif len(unregistered) > 0 || len(orphan) > 0 {\n253|\t\tsort.Strings(unregistered)\n254|\t\tsort.Strings(orphan)\n255|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"digit-guard census mismatch:\\n%s\\n%s\",\n256|\t\t\tstrings.Join(unregistered, \"\\n\"), strings.Join(orphan, \"\\n\"))\n257|\t}\n258|\tt.Logf(\"digit-guard census: %d/%d derived sites rowed across %d production files\",\n259|\t\tlen(sites), len(digitGuardRows), files)\n260|}\n261|\n262|// TestDigitCensusAdjacentsNeverReachGeometryGate proves `/` (0x2F) and\n263|// `:` (0x3A) — the characters adjacent to the digit range — never reach\n264|// the descriptorGeometry gate: neither spells inside a JSON number, so\n265|// the strict decoder refuses first with the document syntax arm. A gate\n266|// mutant shifting either bound (`digit > ':'`, `digit < '/'`) or\n267|// skipping either character token-preservingly changes no disposition\n268|// here; the rows exist so the census claim \"unreachable\" is measured,\n269|// not asserted. Both members are driven because the geometry site is\n270|// shared and the decoder runs before either call.\n271|func TestDigitCensusAdjacentsNeverReachGeometryGate(t *testing.T) {\n272|\tt.Parallel()\n273|\n274|\tfor _, member := range []string{\"columns\", \"rows\"} {\n275|\t\tfor _, literal := range []string{`1/2`, `1:2`} {\n276|\t\t\t_, err := terminalbackend.ParseProviderDescriptor(setDescriptorMember(t, member, literal))\n277|\t\t\tif err == nil || !terminalbackend.IsMismatch(err) {\n278|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ParseProviderDescriptor(%s=%s) error = %v, want a document mismatch refusal\", member, literal, err)\n279|\t\t\t}\n280|\t\t\tif got := refusalDetail(t, err); got != \"document syntax\" {\n281|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ParseProviderDescriptor(%s=%s) detail = %q, want document syntax\", member, literal, got)\n282|\t\t\t}\n283|\t\t}\n284|\t}\n285|}\n286|\n287|// deriveDigitGuardSites parses every production file of the two leaf\n288|// packages and returns every digit-guard site in source order, every\n289|// unclassifiable shape, and the scanned file count. The file set is\n290|// directory-derived: a new production file is scanned without anyone\n291|// remembering it.\n292|func deriveDigitGuardSites(t *testing.T) (sites []digitGuardSite, unclassifiable []string, files int) {\n293|\tt.Helper()\n294|\n295|\troot, err := os.Getwd()\n296|\tif err != nil {\n297|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive digit guards: %v\", err)\n298|\t}\n299|\tdirs := []struct {\n300|\t\tlabel string\n301|\t\tpath  string\n302|\t}{\n303|\t\t{\"terminalbackend\", root},\n304|\t\t{\"provhost\", filepath.Join(root, \"..\", \"provhost\")},\n305|\t}\n306|\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n307|\tfor _, dir := range dirs {\n308|\t\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(dir.path)\n309|\t\tif err != nil {\n310|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive digit guards: read %s: %v\", dir.path, err)\n311|\t\t}\n312|\t\tnames := []string{}\n313|\t\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n314|\t\t\tname := entry.Name()\n315|\t\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(name, \".go\") || strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n316|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n317|\t\t\t}\n318|\t\t\tnames = append(names, name)\n319|\t\t}\n320|\t\tsort.Strings(names)\n321|\t\tfor _, name := range names {\n322|\t\t\tpath := filepath.Join(dir.path, name)\n323|\t\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n324|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n325|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive digit guards: read %s: %v\", path, err)\n326|\t\t\t}\n327|\t\t\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, path, source, 0)\n328|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n329|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive digit guards: parse %s: %v\", path, err)\n330|\t\t\t}\n331|\t\t\tfiles++\n332|\t\t\tfor _, decl := range syntax.Decls {\n333|\t\t\t\tswitch decl := decl.(type) {\n334|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl:\n335|\t\t\t\t\tif decl.Body == nil {\n336|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n337|\t\t\t\t\t}\n338|\t\t\t\t\tfunction := decl.Name.Name\n339|\t\t\t\t\tif decl.Recv != nil && len(decl.Recv.List) > 0 {\n340|\t\t\t\t\t\tfunction = digitGuardReceiver(decl.Recv.List[0].Type) + \".\" + function\n341|\t\t\t\t\t}\n342|\t\t\t\t\tmore, bad := digitGuardSitesInBody(dir.label, name, function, decl.Body)\n343|\t\t\t\t\tsites = append(sites, more...)\n344|\t\t\t\t\tunclassifiable = append(unclassifiable, bad...)\n345|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n346|\t\t\t\t\tmore, bad := digitGuardSitesInInit(dir.label, name, decl)\n347|\t\t\t\t\tsites = append(sites, more...)\n348|\t\t\t\t\tunclassifiable = append(unclassifiable, bad...)\n349|\t\t\t\t}\n350|\t\t\t}\n351|\t\t}\n352|\t}\n353|\tif files == 0 {\n354|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived digit guards from zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the leaf\")\n355|\t}\n356|\tif len(sites) == 0 {\n357|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero digit guards from the leaf sources; the scanner is broken, not the leaf\")\n358|\t}\n359|\treturn sites, unclassifiable, files\n360|}\n361|\n362|// digitGuardReceiver names the receiver type of a method for the site\n363|// key: value and pointer receivers share the key space.\n364|func digitGuardReceiver(expr ast.Expr) string {\n365|\texpr = digitGuardUnparen(expr)\n366|\tif star, ok := expr.(*ast.StarExpr); ok {\n367|\t\treturn digitGuardReceiver(star.X)\n368|\t}\n369|\tif ident, ok := expr.(*ast.Ident); ok {\n370|\t\treturn ident.Name\n371|\t}\n372|\treturn \"recv\"\n373|}\n374|\n375|// digitGuardUnparen strips parentheses.\n376|func digitGuardUnparen(expr ast.Expr) ast.Expr {\n377|\tfor {\n378|\t\tparen, ok := expr.(*ast.ParenExpr)\n379|\t\tif !ok {\n380|\t\t\treturn expr\n381|\t\t}\n382|\t\texpr = paren.X\n383|\t}\n384|}\n385|\n386|// digitGuardSitesInInit scans one package-level declaration with no\n387|// accumulator in scope: only char chains can appear here, and any\n388|// accumulator-shaped comparison fails as unclassifiable rather than\n389|// entering silently.\n390|func digitGuardSitesInInit(dir, file string, decl *ast.GenDecl) ([]digitGuardSite, []string) {\n391|\tvar sites []digitGuardSite\n392|\tvar bad []string\n393|\tast.Inspect(decl, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n394|\t\texpr, ok := node.(ast.Expr)\n395|\t\tif !ok {\n396|\t\t\treturn true\n397|\t\t}\n398|\t\tsite, failure, done := digitGuardClassifyRoot(dir, file, \"(package initializer)\", expr, map[string]bool{})\n399|\t\tif done {\n400|\t\t\tif failure != \"\" {\n401|\t\t\t\tbad = append(bad, failure)\n402|\t\t\t} else if site != nil {\n403|\t\t\t\tsites = append(sites, *site)\n404|\t\t\t}\n405|\t\t\treturn false\n406|\t\t}\n407|\t\treturn true\n408|\t})\n409|\treturn sites, bad\n410|}\n411|\n412|// digitGuardSitesInBody scans one function body. Accumulators are\n413|// collected first so a guard comparison resolves against the\n414|// function's own accumulation steps, never against a name list.\n415|func digitGuardSitesInBody(dir, file, function string, body *ast.BlockStmt) ([]digitGuardSite, []string) {\n416|\taccumulators := digitGuardAccumulators(body)\n417|\tvar sites []digitGuardSite\n418|\tvar bad []string\n419|\tast.Inspect(body, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n420|\t\texpr, ok := node.(ast.Expr)\n421|\t\tif !ok {\n422|\t\t\treturn true\n423|\t\t}\n424|\t\tsite, failure, done := digitGuardClassifyRoot(dir, file, function, expr, accumulators)\n425|\t\tif done {\n426|\t\t\tif failure != \"\" {\n427|\t\t\t\tbad = append(bad, failure)\n428|\t\t\t} else if site != nil {\n429|\t\t\t\tsites = append(sites, *site)\n430|\t\t\t}\n431|\t\t\treturn false\n432|\t\t}\n433|\t\treturn true\n434|\t})\n435|\treturn sites, bad\n436|}\n437|\n438|// digitGuardClassifyRoot decides whether expr is a chain root worth\n439|// classifying: a ||/&& whose parent the Inspect walk already consumed\n440|// is part of the outer chain, and a comparison inside any ||/&&\n441|// chain belongs to its root. Non-root nodes report done=false so the\n442|// walk descends. A root with no digit or accumulator content reports\n443|// done=true with no site, pruning the walk below it.\n444|func digitGuardClassifyRoot(dir, file, function string, expr ast.Expr, accumulators map[string]bool) (*digitGuardSite, string, bool) {\n445|\tbinary, ok := expr.(*ast.BinaryExpr)\n446|\tif !ok {\n447|\t\treturn nil, \"\", false\n448|\t}\n449|\tif binary.Op == token.LOR || binary.Op == token.LAND {\n450|\t\treturn digitGuardClassifyChain(dir, file, function, binary, accumulators)\n451|\t}\n452|\tif digitGuardIsComparison(binary.Op) {\n453|\t\tleaf := digitGuardClassifyLeaf(binary, accumulators)\n454|\t\tswitch leaf {\n455|\t\tcase digitLeafChar:\n456|\t\t\treturn &digitGuardSite{dir: dir, file: file, function: function, kind: \"char\", expr: digitGuardCanon(binary)}, \"\", true\n457|\t\tcase digitLeafBound:\n458|\t\t\treturn &digitGuardSite{dir: dir, file: file, function: function, kind: \"bound\", expr: digitGuardCanon(binary)}, \"\", true\n459|\t\tcase digitLeafBad:\n460|\t\t\treturn nil, \"unclassifiable guard in \" + file + \" (\" + function + \"): \" + digitGuardCanon(binary), true\n461|\t\tdefault:\n462|\t\t\treturn nil, \"\", false\n463|\t\t}\n464|\t}\n465|\treturn nil, \"\", false\n466|}\n467|\n468|// digitGuardClassifyChain gathers the leaves of one maximal ||/&&\n469|// chain and places the chain: pure digit chains are char sites,\n470|// pure accumulator chains are bound sites, anything mixed or\n471|// degenerate is unclassifiable, and chains with no digit or\n472|// accumulator content are pruned.\n473|func digitGuardClassifyChain(dir, file, function string, root *ast.BinaryExpr, accumulators map[string]bool) (*digitGuardSite, string, bool) {\n474|\tvar chars, bounds, other, bad int\n475|\tvar visit func(expr ast.Expr)\n476|\tvisit = func(expr ast.Expr) {\n477|\t\texpr = digitGuardUnparen(expr)\n478|\t\tif inner, ok := expr.(*ast.BinaryExpr); ok && (inner.Op == token.LOR || inner.Op == token.LAND) {\n479|\t\t\tvisit(inner.X)\n480|\t\t\tvisit(inner.Y)\n481|\t\t\treturn\n482|\t\t}\n483|\t\tif negated, ok := expr.(*ast.UnaryExpr); ok && negated.Op == token.NOT {\n484|\t\t\tif digitGuardMentionsDigitOrAccumulator(negated.X, accumulators) {\n485|\t\t\t\tbad++\n486|\t\t\t} else {\n487|\t\t\t\tother++\n488|\t\t\t}\n489|\t\t\treturn\n490|\t\t}\n491|\t\tif comparison, ok := expr.(*ast.BinaryExpr); ok && digitGuardIsComparison(comparison.Op) {\n492|\t\t\tswitch digitGuardClassifyLeaf(comparison, accumulators) {\n493|\t\t\tcase digitLeafChar:\n494|\t\t\t\tchars++\n495|\t\t\tcase digitLeafBound:\n496|\t\t\t\tbounds++\n497|\t\t\tcase digitLeafBad:\n498|\t\t\t\tbad++\n499|\t\t\tdefault:\n500|\t\t\t\tother++\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c541","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0798e-8ce3-71d2-82cf-4115ffc6a2dc"},"sequence":251,"recorded_at":1780531400000497,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a"},"call_id":"call_01a0798f15007191a082a88139f24247","text":"Read text file `internal/provhost/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"context\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\t\"errors\"\n7|\t\"fmt\"\n8|\t\"go/ast\"\n9|\t\"go/parser\"\n10|\t\"go/token\"\n11|\t\"os\"\n12|\t\"path/filepath\"\n13|\t\"sort\"\n14|\t\"strconv\"\n15|\t\"strings\"\n16|\t\"testing\"\n17|\t\"time\"\n18|\n19|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n20|)\n21|\n22|// This file is the derived refusal-arm inventory. It exists because the\n23|// constructor call-site audit in inventory_test.go enumerates constructor\n24|// call SITES, and every frameFault literal and every integrity(...) detail\n25|// funnels through a shared site: planting a new arm through an existing\n26|// site (a new &frameFault literal in checkResponseMembers, a new\n27|// integrity(...) detail in DecodeStatusOutcome) leaves the whole suite\n28|// green. Two review rounds each missed a row by hand, so the arm set is\n29|// derived from production source by parsing it, never by listing it.\n30|//\n31|// Derivation (deriveRefusalArms): every &frameFault{...} literal yields\n32|// frame|<detail>|<member source>; every integrity(...) call with a string\n33|// literal yields integrity|<detail>; the single wrapping site\n34|// integrity(\"status body is \"+fault.detail, ...) expands over the derived\n35|// frame detail set, so each wrapped refusal is its own obligation; every\n36|// rejection branch of parseMajor (a return 0, false) yields\n37|// parse|<enclosing condition source>; every literal first argument to one\n38|// of the six refusal constructors yields ctor|<constructor>|<detail>.\n39|// A non-literal frameFault detail or integrity argument lands as an\n40|// expr:<source> obligation rather than passing silently; a non-literal\n41|// constructor first argument is a fault conduit (fault.detail, a detail\n42|// variable) whose arms are the frame arms above, so it carries no\n43|// separate obligation by design. A missing parseMajor fails the\n44|// derivation outright.\n45|//\n46|// Both directions are checked: TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed\n47|// (every derived arm carries a witness) and\n48|// TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived (every witness names a derived arm, so a\n49|// truncated derivation reddens on the orphaned witnesses instead of\n50|// passing vacuously). TestEveryArmWitnessRefusesAtTheProductionEntry\n51|// drives each witness through the production entry and requires the\n52|// refusal to come from the arm under test. Empty, single-file, or\n53|// unparseable derivations fail closed: a domain that silently derives\n54|// nothing is not a measurement.\n55|//\n56|// Stated bound: arms sharing one (constructor, detail) identity merge to\n57|// one obligation (the two timeout sites, the two empty-response sites,\n58|// the six identical \"not a JSON object\" sites). Deleting one of a merged\n59|// pair is a behavioral mutant the entry-point tests must catch, not this\n60|// inventory.\n61|\n62|// refusalArmCensusFloor is the derived arm count this test was written\n63|// against. It is a tripwire, not an enumeration: a derivation returning\n64|// fewer arms fails closed even when every surviving arm is witnessed,\n65|// which is what catches a silently truncated scan. Raising it is routine\n66|// when production gains a refusal; lowering it requires saying why.\n67|//\n68|// Raised 60 -> 162 by the operation-layer leaf (manifest, probe,\n69|// profile, quiescence, spawn, identity, idempotency decoders), each\n70|// new arm witnessed in declaredOperationWitnesses below, then 162 ->\n71|// 164 by the lone-surrogate gate and 164 -> 166 by the UTF-8 gate:\n72|// one frame arm in decodeStrictObject plus its status-body integrity\n73|// expansion each, every one witnessed above.\n74|const refusalArmCensusFloor = 166\n75|\n76|func deriveRefusalArms(t *testing.T) map[string]struct{} {\n77|\tt.Helper()\n78|\tdirectory, err := os.Getwd()\n79|\tif err != nil {\n80|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive refusal arms: %v\", err)\n81|\t}\n82|\tarms, scanned, err := refusalArmsIn(directory)\n83|\tif err != nil {\n84|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive refusal arms: %v\", err)\n85|\t}\n86|\tif len(scanned) == 0 {\n87|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived refusal arms from zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n88|\t}\n89|\tif len(arms) == 0 {\n90|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero refusal arms from the package sources; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n91|\t}\n92|\tif len(arms) < refusalArmCensusFloor {\n93|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived %d refusal arms, below the %d census floor; the derivation is short, not the package\", len(arms), refusalArmCensusFloor)\n94|\t}\n95|\tt.Logf(\"refusal arm coverage domain: %d derived arms across %d production files\", len(arms), len(scanned))\n96|\treturn arms\n97|}\n98|\n99|func refusalArmsIn(directory string) (map[string]struct{}, []string, error) {\n100|\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(directory)\n101|\tif err != nil {\n102|\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n103|\t}\n104|\tarms := map[string]struct{}{}\n105|\tvar scanned []string\n106|\tparseBranches := 0\n107|\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n108|\ttype productionFile struct {\n109|\t\tsyntax *ast.File\n110|\t\tsource []byte\n111|\t}\n112|\tvar files []productionFile\n113|\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n114|\t\tname := entry.Name()\n115|\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(name, \".go\") || strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n116|\t\t\tcontinue\n117|\t\t}\n118|\t\tscanned = append(scanned, name)\n119|\t\tpath := filepath.Join(directory, name)\n120|\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n121|\t\tif err != nil {\n122|\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n123|\t\t}\n124|\t\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, path, source, parser.ParseComments)\n125|\t\tif err != nil {\n126|\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n127|\t\t}\n128|\t\tfiles = append(files, productionFile{syntax: syntax, source: source})\n129|\t}\n130|\t// First pass, package-wide: the decodeStrictObject fault detail\n131|\t// set, which the integrity wrapper site expands over. The wrapper\n132|\t// only wraps decodeStrictObject faults, so checkResponseMembers\n133|\t// arms (\"missing member\", \"unknown member\", ...) are not in this\n134|\t// set: expanding over every frameFault literal would invent arms\n135|\t// production can never emit. The pass must span files because the\n136|\t// literals live in protocol.go while the wrapper lives in status.go.\n137|\tvar strictDetails []string\n138|\tseenDetail := map[string]bool{}\n139|\tfor _, file := range files {\n140|\t\tfor _, decl := range file.syntax.Decls {\n141|\t\t\tfunction, ok := decl.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n142|\t\t\tif !ok || function.Name.Name != \"decodeStrictObject\" {\n143|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n144|\t\t\t}\n145|\t\t\tast.Inspect(function.Body, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n146|\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := frameFaultLiteral(node)\n147|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n148|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n149|\t\t\t\t}\n150|\t\t\t\tdetail, ok := literalStringField(file.source, fileSet, literal, \"detail\")\n151|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n152|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n153|\t\t\t\t}\n154|\t\t\t\tif !seenDetail[detail] {\n155|\t\t\t\t\tseenDetail[detail] = true\n156|\t\t\t\t\tstrictDetails = append(strictDetails, detail)\n157|\t\t\t\t}\n158|\t\t\t\treturn true\n159|\t\t\t})\n160|\t\t}\n161|\t}\n162|\tfor _, file := range files {\n163|\t\tsource, syntax := file.source, file.syntax\n164|\t\tparseBranches += armParseBranches(source, fileSet, syntax, arms)\n165|\t\tast.Inspect(syntax, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n166|\t\t\tif literal, ok := frameFaultLiteral(node); ok {\n167|\t\t\t\tdetail, ok := literalStringField(source, fileSet, literal, \"detail\")\n168|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n169|\t\t\t\t\tarms[\"frame|expr:\"+nodeSource(source, fileSet, node)] = struct{}{}\n170|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n171|\t\t\t\t}\n172|\t\t\t\tmember := \"\"\n173|\t\t\t\tif kv := literalField(literal, \"member\"); kv != nil {\n174|\t\t\t\t\tmember = nodeSource(source, fileSet, kv.Value)\n175|\t\t\t\t}\n176|\t\t\t\tarms[\"frame|\"+detail+\"|\"+member] = struct{}{}\n177|\t\t\t\treturn true\n178|\t\t\t}\n179|\t\t\tcall, ok := node.(*ast.CallExpr)\n180|\t\t\tif !ok {\n181|\t\t\t\treturn true\n182|\t\t\t}\n183|\t\t\tident, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.Ident)\n184|\t\t\tif !ok || len(call.Args) == 0 {\n185|\t\t\t\treturn true\n186|\t\t\t}\n187|\t\t\tswitch ident.Name {\n188|\t\t\tcase \"integrity\":\n189|\t\t\t\tif literal, ok := call.Args[0].(*ast.BasicLit); ok && literal.Kind == token.STRING {\n190|\t\t\t\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n191|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n192|\t\t\t\t\t\tarms[\"integrity|expr:\"+nodeSource(source, fileSet, call.Args[0])] = struct{}{}\n193|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n194|\t\t\t\t\t}\n195|\t\t\t\t\tarms[\"integrity|\"+detail] = struct{}{}\n196|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n197|\t\t\t\t}\n198|\t\t\t\tif prefix, ok := integrityPrefix(call.Args[0]); ok {\n199|\t\t\t\t\tif len(strictDetails) == 0 {\n200|\t\t\t\t\t\tarms[\"integrity|expr:\"+nodeSource(source, fileSet, call.Args[0])] = struct{}{}\n201|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n202|\t\t\t\t\t}\n203|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, detail := range strictDetails {\n204|\t\t\t\t\t\tarms[\"integrity|\"+prefix+detail] = struct{}{}\n205|\t\t\t\t\t}\n206|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n207|\t\t\t\t}\n208|\t\t\t\tarms[\"integrity|expr:\"+nodeSource(source, fileSet, call.Args[0])] = struct{}{}\n209|\t\t\tcase \"failInvalid\", \"failProtocol\", \"failMismatch\", \"failProcess\", \"failTimeout\":\n210|\t\t\t\tif literal, ok := call.Args[0].(*ast.BasicLit); ok && literal.Kind == token.STRING {\n211|\t\t\t\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n212|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n213|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n214|\t\t\t\t\t}\n215|\t\t\t\t\tarms[\"ctor|\"+ident.Name+\"|\"+detail] = struct{}{}\n216|\t\t\t\t}\n217|\t\t\t\t// Non-literal first arguments are the fault conduits\n218|\t\t\t\t// (fault.detail, detail variables): the arms behind\n219|\t\t\t\t// them are the frame arms above, so there is no\n220|\t\t\t\t// separate obligation here.\n221|\t\t\t}\n222|\t\t\treturn true\n223|\t\t})\n224|\t}\n225|\tif parseBranches == 0 {\n226|\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"parseMajor carries no rejection branch anywhere; the classification-branch enumeration is blind\")\n227|\t}\n228|\tsort.Strings(scanned)\n229|\treturn arms, scanned, nil\n230|}\n231|\n232|// frameFaultLiteral reports whether node is a &frameFault{...} literal.\n233|func frameFaultLiteral(node ast.Node) (*ast.CompositeLit, bool) {\n234|\ttarget := node\n235|\tif unary, ok := node.(*ast.UnaryExpr); ok && unary.Op == token.AND {\n236|\t\ttarget = unary.X\n237|\t}\n238|\tliteral, ok := target.(*ast.CompositeLit)\n239|\tif !ok {\n240|\t\treturn nil, false\n241|\t}\n242|\tident, ok := literal.Type.(*ast.Ident)\n243|\tif !ok || ident.Name != \"frameFault\" {\n244|\t\treturn nil, false\n245|\t}\n246|\treturn literal, true\n247|}\n248|\n249|func literalField(literal *ast.CompositeLit, name string) *ast.KeyValueExpr {\n250|\tfor _, element := range literal.Elts {\n251|\t\tif kv, ok := element.(*ast.KeyValueExpr); ok {\n252|\t\t\tif ident, ok := kv.Key.(*ast.Ident); ok && ident.Name == name {\n253|\t\t\t\treturn kv\n254|\t\t\t}\n255|\t\t}\n256|\t}\n257|\treturn nil\n258|}\n259|\n260|func literalStringField(source []byte, fileSet *token.FileSet, literal *ast.CompositeLit, name string) (string, bool) {\n261|\tkv := literalField(literal, name)\n262|\tif kv == nil {\n263|\t\treturn \"\", false\n264|\t}\n265|\tbasic, ok := kv.Value.(*ast.BasicLit)\n266|\tif !ok || basic.Kind != token.STRING {\n267|\t\treturn \"\", false\n268|\t}\n269|\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(basic.Value)\n270|\tif err != nil {\n271|\t\treturn \"\", false\n272|\t}\n273|\treturn detail, true\n274|}\n275|\n276|// integrityPrefix matches \"prefix\" + <expr>, the wrapping shape whose\n277|// arms expand over the derived frame detail set.\n278|func integrityPrefix(arg ast.Expr) (string, bool) {\n279|\tbinary, ok := arg.(*ast.BinaryExpr)\n280|\tif !ok || binary.Op != token.ADD {\n281|\t\treturn \"\", false\n282|\t}\n283|\tprefix, ok := binary.X.(*ast.BasicLit)\n284|\tif !ok || prefix.Kind != token.STRING {\n285|\t\treturn \"\", false\n286|\t}\n287|\ttext, err := strconv.Unquote(prefix.Value)\n288|\tif err != nil {\n289|\t\treturn \"\", false\n290|\t}\n291|\treturn text, true\n292|}\n293|\n294|func nodeSource(source []byte, fileSet *token.FileSet, node ast.Node) string {\n295|\tstart := fileSet.Position(node.Pos()).Offset\n296|\tend := fileSet.Position(node.End()).Offset\n297|\tif start < 0 || end > len(source) || start >= end {\n298|\t\treturn \"?\"\n299|\t}\n300|\treturn strings.Join(strings.Fields(string(source[start:end])), \" \")\n301|}\n302|\n303|// armParseBranches derives one obligation per parseMajor rejection\n304|// branch in this file: every return 0, false inside parseMajor, keyed by\n305|// its innermost enclosing condition, and returns how many it derived. A\n306|// new branch adds a key no witness names; a deleted branch orphans its\n307|// witness; narrowing || to && rewrites the key and does both. The caller\n308|// fails closed when no file derives any branch.\n309|func armParseBranches(source []byte, fileSet *token.FileSet, syntax *ast.File, arms map[string]struct{}) int {\n310|\tvar body *ast.BlockStmt\n311|\tfor _, decl := range syntax.Decls {\n312|\t\tfunction, ok := decl.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n313|\t\tif ok && function.Name.Name == \"parseMajor\" {\n314|\t\t\tbody = function.Body\n315|\t\t}\n316|\t}\n317|\tif body == nil {\n318|\t\treturn 0\n319|\t}\n320|\tcount := 0\n321|\tvar conditions []string\n322|\tvar walk func(node ast.Node)\n323|\twalk = func(node ast.Node) {\n324|\t\tbranch, ok := node.(*ast.IfStmt)\n325|\t\tif !ok {\n326|\t\t\tfor _, child := range childNodes(node) {\n327|\t\t\t\twalk(child)\n328|\t\t\t}\n329|\t\t\treturn\n330|\t\t}\n331|\t\tconditions = append(conditions, nodeSource(source, fileSet, branch.Cond))\n332|\t\tfor _, stmt := range branch.Body.List {\n333|\t\t\tif ret, ok := stmt.(*ast.ReturnStmt); ok && isFalsePair(ret) {\n334|\t\t\t\tarms[\"parse|\"+conditions[len(conditions)-1]] = struct{}{}\n335|\t\t\t\tcount++\n336|\t\t\t}\n337|\t\t}\n338|\t\tfor _, child := range childNodes(node) {\n339|\t\t\twalk(child)\n340|\t\t}\n341|\t\tconditions = conditions[:len(conditions)-1]\n342|\t}\n343|\twalk(body)\n344|\treturn count\n345|}\n346|\n347|func isFalsePair(ret *ast.ReturnStmt) bool {\n348|\tif len(ret.Results) != 2 {\n349|\t\treturn false\n350|\t}\n351|\tzero, ok := ret.Results[0].(*ast.BasicLit)\n352|\tif !ok || zero.Kind != token.INT || zero.Value != \"0\" {\n353|\t\treturn false\n354|\t}\n355|\tno, ok := ret.Results[1].(*ast.Ident)\n356|\treturn ok && no.Name == \"false\"\n357|}\n358|\n359|func childNodes(node ast.Node) []ast.Node {\n360|\tvar children []ast.Node\n361|\tast.Inspect(node, func(child ast.Node) bool {\n362|\t\tif child == nil || child == node {\n363|\t\t\treturn true\n364|\t\t}\n365|\t\tchildren = append(children, child)\n366|\t\treturn false\n367|\t})\n368|\treturn children\n369|}\n370|\n371|// armWitness proves one derived refusal arm at the production entry.\n372|// The arm key must equal the derived key exactly: TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived\n373|// fails a witness that names nothing production declares, so a deleted or\n374|// narrowed production branch orphans its witness instead of passing\n375|// silently. The prove function must drive the production entry point and\n376|// require the refusal attributed to THIS arm, not merely any refusal.\n377|type armWitness struct {\n378|\tarm   string\n379|\tname  string\n380|\tprove func(*testing.T)\n381|}\n382|\n383|// requireIntegrityRefusal asserts the full identity of a status refusal:\n384|// the integrity_failure code, the rule detail, the status_state detail\n385|// every integrity arm carries (AS6: asserted on all 18 arms, not just\n386|// the unknown row), exit 9, and the non-retryable bit. It is separate\n387|// from requireLocalRefusal because that helper also serves codes with no\n388|// status_state detail.\n389|func requireIntegrityRefusal(t *testing.T, err error, detail, wantState string) {\n390|\tt.Helper()\n391|\trequireLocalRefusal(t, err, \"integrity_failure\", detail)\n392|\tstate, ok := failureObject(t, err).Detail(\"status_state\")\n393|\tif !ok || state != wantState {\n394|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"integrity refusal status_state = %v, want %q (%v)\", state, wantState, err)\n395|\t}\n396|\tif failureExit(t, err) != 9 {\n397|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"integrity refusal exit = %d, want 9\", failureExit(t, err))\n398|\t}\n399|}\n400|\n401|func armVersionFrame(version string) []byte {\n402|\treturn []byte(`{\"protocol\":\"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\"protocol_version\":\"` + version + `\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID + `\",\"ok\":true,\"body\":{}}`)\n403|}\n404|\n405|func armMemberFrame(members string) []byte {\n406|\treturn []byte(`{\"protocol\":\"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\"protocol_version\":\"2.0.0\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID + `\",` + members + `}`)\n407|}\n408|\n409|func armOversizeResponse(t *testing.T) []byte {\n410|\tt.Helper()\n411|\tbuild := func(pad int) []byte {\n412|\t\treturn successFrame(t, testRequestID, `{\"pad\":\"`+strings.Repeat(\"a\", pad)+`\"}`)\n413|\t}\n414|\tbase := len(build(0))\n415|\tover := build(specFrameLimitBytes - base + 1)\n416|\tif len(over) != specFrameLimitBytes+1 {\n417|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"oversize fixture is %d bytes, want exactly %d\", len(over), specFrameLimitBytes+1)\n418|\t}\n419|\treturn over\n420|}\n421|\n422|func declaredArmWitnesses() []armWitness {\n423|\treturn []armWitness{\n424|\t\t// decodeStrictObject frame arms, through DecodeResponse.\n425|\t\t{arm: `frame|not a JSON object|\"\"`, name: \"array is not an object\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n426|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse([]byte(`[1,2]`), mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n427|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"\", \"not a JSON object\")\n428|\t\t}},\n429|\t\t{arm: `frame|not a JSON object|key`, name: \"truncated value names its member\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n430|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse([]byte(`{\"protocol\":`), mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n431|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"protocol\", \"not a JSON object\")\n432|\t\t}},\n433|\t\t{arm: `frame|duplicate member|key`, name: \"repeated member\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n434|\t\t\tframe := []byte(`{\"protocol\":\"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\"protocol_version\":\"2.0.0\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID + `\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID + `\",\"ok\":true,\"body\":{}}`)\n435|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(frame, mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n436|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"request_id\", \"duplicate member\")\n437|\t\t}},\n438|\t\t{arm: `frame|trailing data after the object|\"\"`, name: \"trailing byte\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n439|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(append(successFrame(t, testRequestID, `{\"provider_id\":\"pi\"}`), 'x'), mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n440|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"\", \"trailing data after the object\")\n441|\t\t}},\n442|\t\t{arm: `frame|lone surrogate escape|\"\"`, name: \"lone surrogate in body\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n443|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(successFrame(t, testRequestID, `{\"provider_id\":\"pi\",\"tag\":\"a\\ud800b\"}`), mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n444|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"\", \"lone surrogate escape\")\n445|\t\t}},\n446|\t\t{arm: `frame|not valid UTF-8|\"\"`, name: \"raw bytes in body\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n447|\t\t\terr := DecodeManifest([]byte(\"{\\\"note\\\":\\\"ab\\xffcd\\\"}\"))\n448|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"\", \"not valid UTF-8\")\n449|\t\t}},\n450|\t\t{arm: `frame|missing member|name`, name: \"missing protocol\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n451|\t\t\tframe := []byte(`{\"protocol_version\":\"2.0.0\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID + `\",\"ok\":true,\"body\":{}}`)\n452|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(frame, mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n453|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"protocol\", \"missing member\")\n454|\t\t}},\n455|\t\t{arm: `frame|missing member|\"body\"`, name: \"success without body\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n456|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(armMemberFrame(`\"ok\":true`), mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n457|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"body\", \"missing member\")\n458|\t\t}},\n459|\t\t{arm: `frame|success envelope carries error|\"error\"`, name: \"error on success\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n460|\t\t\tframe := []byte(`{\"protocol\":\"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\"protocol_version\":\"2.0.0\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID + `\",\"ok\":true,\"body\":{},\"error\":{\"schema\":\"urn:ax:schema:error\",\"schema_version\":\"1.0.0\",\"code\":\"capability_unavailable\",\"message\":\"m\",\"exit_code\":6,\"retryable\":false,\"details\":{}}}`)\n461|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(frame, mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n462|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"error\", \"success envelope carries error\")\n463|\t\t}},\n464|\t\t{arm: `frame|missing member|\"error\"`, name: \"failure without error\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n465|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(armMemberFrame(`\"ok\":false`), mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n466|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"error\", \"missing member\")\n467|\t\t}},\n468|\t\t{arm: `frame|failure envelope carries body|\"body\"`, name: \"body on failure\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n469|\t\t\tframe := []byte(`{\"protocol\":\"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\"protocol_version\":\"2.0.0\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID