Names {\n350|\t\t\t\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(name.Name, \"Code\") || index >= len(value.Values) {\n351|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n352|\t\t\t\t\t}\n353|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := value.Values[index].(*ast.BasicLit)\n354|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n355|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"code symbol %s is not a static string; \"+\n356|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"wire codes must be literals\", name.Name)\n357|\t\t\t\t\t}\n358|\t\t\t\t\twire, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n359|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n360|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unquote %s: %v\", name.Name, err)\n361|\t\t\t\t\t}\n362|\t\t\t\t\tsymbols[name.Name] = wire\n363|\t\t\t\t}\n364|\t\t\t}\n365|\t\t}\n366|\t}\n367|\tif len(symbols) == 0 {\n368|\t\tt.Fatal(\"resolved zero code symbols; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n369|\t}\n370|\treturn symbols\n371|}\n372|\n373|// declaredRefusalArm is one inventoried arm: the derived key (file,\n374|// function, code symbol, static detail, occurrence), the public\n375|// production entry its witness drives, an optional stated bound for\n376|// arms no input can reach, and the funneled detail set (nil except the\n377|// funnel row). Non-bound rows are proved by the executed witness of the\n378|// same identity in refusal_arm_witnesses_test.go; bound rows are proved\n379|// by their pinning tests in the pinned set below.\n380|type declaredRefusalArm struct {\n381|\tfile       string\n382|\tfunction   string\n383|\tcode       string\n384|\tdetail     string\n385|\toccurrence int\n386|\tentry      string\n387|\tbound      string\n388|\t// detailSet carries the funneled detail set for the single\n389|\t// dynamic-detail row; it is empty for every literal row.\n390|\tdetailSet []string\n391|}\n392|\n393|// boundDefensiveReparse is the stated bound for re-parse arms after an\n394|// already-validated member: timestampMember validated the member, and the\n395|// Time re-parse cannot fail while scalar owns that contract. The arms\n396|// stay as fail-closed defense; the bound says why no document reaches\n397|// them, and TestDefensiveBoundsAreExactlyThese pins the set.\n398|const boundDefensiveReparse = \"defensive re-parse after validation; scalar owns the re-parse contract\"\n399|\n400|// boundUnreachableVocabulary is the stated bound for CheckTransition's\n401|// \"operation vocabulary\" arm: CheckTransition parses its operation\n402|// through ParseOperation first, and lookupTransition covers every\n(more lines below)"}}}
