{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000f5d9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0798e-8ce3-71d2-82cf-4115ffc6a2dc"},"sequence":6471,"recorded_at":1780531400012937,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"36d0cd2b-2881-45a8-88f5-cfa7779fd40f"},"task_id":"36d0cd2b-2881-45a8-88f5-cfa7779fd40f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"36d0cd2b-2881-45a8-88f5-cfa7779fd40f","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/EPIC-260830-37rgqn_m0-contract-foundation/STORY-260905-3t31e9_cross-story-identity-ownership-and-inventory-consolidation/TASK-260906-v8heil_unify-inventory-machinery-on-executed-witnesses/README.md`.\n1|# TASK-260906-v8heil: unify-inventory-machinery-on-executed-witnesses\n2|\n3|## Description\n4|Close advisory A6. Twenty hand-rolled go/parser walkers now exist across ten packages, seven added by the two landed Stories, in three architectures for the same idea: terminalbackend resolves a declared row textually (a row passes if the named test source mentions the detail, so a dead arm can resolve through a sibling and the file says so); provhost executes every witness through the production entry point and requires the refusal to come from that arm; provider swaps constructor vars in TestMain and audits the exercised file:line set against AST-derived sites. The weaker bound is the real bound. Extract a shared test-support core carrying the production-file glob, fail-closed parse, and a both-direction check harness, and port terminalbackend from textual resolution to executed witnesses. Each existing walker closes a different blind spot (terminalbackend refuses constructor aliasing outright, provider catches aliases at runtime, provhost keys on identifier names and relies on a separate call-site audit); the shared core must keep the union of those, not the intersection.\n5|\n6|## Scope\n7|relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0 (commit 28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c). Resolve seams found by the consolidated cross-Story review (.temp/fable-consolidated-review.md). Work only inside the cross-story-identity-ownership-and-inventory-consistency story boundary. Preserve all stronger existing invariants; no gate may be weakened to close a seam.\n8|\n9|## Acceptance Criteria\n10|Production behavior demonstrates: one shared test-support core owns production-file selection, fail-closed parsing, and the both-direction harness, and every existing inventory is expressed through it. terminalbackend refusal arms are resolved by executed witnesses that refuse at the production entry point, not by source text mentioning a detail string. Alias-bypass coverage is preserved for every package that had it, proven by a negative test per bypass shape that fails when the core drops that direction. Arm counts before and after are reported with any change accounted for; a floor regresses no package."}}}
