bility ownership registry\\n21:- [x] A v3 envelope reaching provhost produces the documented outcome, driven in both directions: admitted where the owner accepts it and refused with the named arm where it does not\\n22:- [x] The Error 1.3.0 binding for v3 is either implemented or an explicit stated bound names the deferring task; protocol.go no longer binds major 2 to Error 1.0.0 silently for v3\\n23:- [x] A provider discovery failure lifts into an axerror Structured Error through a production path that axerror accepts, proven by driving the real lift\\n24:- [x] A negative test shows a causal-leak shape is refused; no machine-local path, provider ID or owner identity reaches any wire message\\n25:- [x] CheckProviderDescriptor is completed or relocated to the named owner, and the traceability registry records which package owns 7.A\\n26:- [x] Every census or roster derives its denominator from production and fails closed on an unregistered site, an orphan row, an import alias and a var-binding, each control-planted\\n27:- [x] Mutation battery reports killed over applied on a production-derived denominator with narrowing, arm-deletion and census-only separate, and NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL as distinct rows\\n28:- [x] Candidate tree OID in the outcome document equals the one the Change Request record carries, verified by listing the tree\\n29:- [x] Code written per task description and AC\\n30:- [x] Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\n31:- [x] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\n32:- [x] Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\n33:- [x] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\n34:- [x] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\n35:- [x] Lint clean\\n36:- [x] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\n37:- [x] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\n38:- [x] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\n39:- [x] Implementation matches AC\\n40:- [x] Solution fits project architecture\\n41:- [x] Tests green\\n42:- [x] Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\\n43:- [x] If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3731,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 933,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
