{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000001043f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0798e-8ce3-71d2-82cf-4115ffc6a2dc"},"sequence":8314,"recorded_at":1780531400016623,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f7e88212-ef87-40d2-a1db-8797ebe2238a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"63ae0568-248e-4ff8-8f32-4d4f1d8c0a14"},"task_id":"63ae0568-248e-4ff8-8f32-4d4f1d8c0a14","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"63ae0568-248e-4ff8-8f32-4d4f1d8c0a14","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-374-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cd /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260905-3t31e9/worktree && head -n 40 LOGBOOK.md; date \\\"+%Y-%m-%d %H%M\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Read logbook head and current time\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-06\\n\\n### 2255 — review round 6: listing census replaced by one derived enumeration over both digit-guard shapes (F1/F2)\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (fourth consecutive round of the digit-edge class). No production change. Deleted `terminalbackend/digit_range_census_test.go` (listed its own sites, scoped out the accumulation bounds); new `terminalbackend/digit_guard_census_test.go` derives 9 sites in one AST pass over terminalbackend+provhost production — char (ordering vs a digit rune, incl. hex digit cases) and bound (ordering vs a same-function `*10` accumulator) — keyed structurally (rune values, accumulation steps, printer-normalized chains), with per-site rows (rejected class / threshold+witness) and three fail-closed arms (unregistered, orphan, unclassifiable). F1 witness: the 37-digit `9223372036854775808000000000000000001` on both geometry members (fails under the `> 922337203685477580` edge mutant, green at 100/1000/1e9/92233720368547758).\\n- FINDING (battery corrected the work, in-session): the first battery run left the hex token-preserving inserts (manifest `case digit == ':'`, surrogate `b == ':'`) SURVIVED with the condition edits census-only — the canonical-JSON sweeps never probe `:` inside an escape. New `TestDocumentHexEscapeDigitBoundaryRefused` / `TestProductionEntriesRefuseHexDigitBoundaryEscapes` drive `\\\\ud80:`/`\\\\udc0:` (malformed→syntax arm on real code, completing 0xD80A/0xDC0A lone surrogates under the mutant); both inserts are now BEHAVIORAL-ONLY kills with census exit 0. Lower edge (`/`) converts to 0xFFFF no surrogate prefix survives: widened lower bounds are verdict-equivalent on every input, measured by R6-D32/R6-D33 (behavioural green, census red) — a stated bound with a measurement, not prose.\\n- FINDING: the census keys survive renaming by construction — control plants prove it: a var-bound gate fails as `…|plantVarBindingTmp|char|octet < '0' || octet > '9'`, an import-aliased file as an unregistered site, plus plain/orphan/`== '5'`/bound plants; all six redden only the census test and revert SHA-256-clean.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round6.md` on the board task (9-site table, 33-row mutant table with per-arm split, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`); harness `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_mut-round6.py` + `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_battery-round6.json` + `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_plants-round6.py` + `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_plants-round6.json` attached as task resources.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs, 0 FAIL), `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 86.0%, terminalbackend 94.3%), `go vet` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 36 sections, 98 cases), `GOOS=windows go build/vet` exit 0, `-race` exit 0 on provhost + terminalbackend. Battery: 33 applied / 33 killed / 0 survivors (narrowing 16/16, token-preserving 8/8 all behavioural-only, arm-deletion 9/9) + census-only C01 + NOT_APPLIED + COMPILE_FAIL as distinct rows; masks calibrated non-empty (census 2 RUN, behavioural 460/671 RUN, all green pristine).\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2254 — review round 5: saturation edge carried to semverMajor, geometry upper window closed, three-site digit census recorded (F1/F2)\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (third consecutive round of the digit-edge class; the two new sites are both inside this leaf's delta in `internal/terminalbackend`). No production change: the `semverMajor` guard and the `descriptorGeometry` gate were already correct. Tests: new `TestSemverMajorSaturationEdge` (largest exact fit 9223372036854775807, +1, aliasing witness 922337203685477580801.0.0 ±1, each requiring semverMajor==MaxInt AND refusal at ParseProviderDescriptor/CheckVersionTuple with the named arm, plus the witness at New); `1E2` rows on columns and rows in the value-refusals table; new `digit_range_census_test.go` recording all three leaf digit-range comparisons with per-site reachable rejected classes and declared equivalents, plus `TestDescriptorGeometryAdjacentsNeverReachTheGate` (`/`/`:` die at document syntax before the gate).\\n- FINDING (measured): weakened guard `major > math.MaxInt/10` admits 922337203685477580801.0.0 at ParseProviderDescriptor with err=nil (semverMajor returns 1, aliasing native major 1); weakened bound `digit > 'E'` admits `columns: 1E2` as Columns=312; both survived the whole 457-test suite. The neighbours refuse either way, so the value pins (==MaxInt) carry those kills — the round-4 lesson, re-applied. `+` is a declared equivalent (only legal after e/E, which refuses first); `/` and `:` are provably unreachable through json.Number.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round5.md` on the board task (F1/F2 tables, 9-mutant battery with behavioural-vs-census split per arm, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`); harness `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_mut-round5.py` + `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_battery-round5.json` attached as task resources.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs, 0 FAIL), `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 85.8%, terminalbackend 94.2%), `go vet` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 36 sections, 98 cases), `GOOS=windows go build/vet` exit 0, `-race` exit 0 on provhost + terminalbackend. Battery: 9 applied / 8 killed / 1 survived (T-D3 `+`, declared equivalent) + NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL as distinct control rows; the token-preserving narrowings (T-D1 killed, T-D3 equivalent, re-pinned P-M17 killed) all show zero census kill, and the arm-deletion T-D4 co-fires the census pair by construction.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2253 — review round 4: parse-gate edges pinned behaviourally, census-only kills closed (F1a/F1b)\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (F1a saturation-edge + F1b digit-range token-preserving, N4 peek-widening, N6 test-bound placement). No production change: `provhost/protocol.go` guard was already correct. Tests: new `TestParseMajorSaturationEdge` (MaxInt, MaxInt+1, aliasing witness 922337203685477580802.0.0 ±1, each requiring parseMajor==MaxInt AND DecodeResponse incompatible_protocol/exit 6), new `TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry` ('/' 0x2F and ':' 0x3A in major and in each rest position, each requiring parseMajor unrecognized AND DecodeResponse provider_protocol_error/exit 13), new `TestDecodeResponseUnrecognizedVersionRunsMemberRules` (bare-frame member `ok` pins the peek widening). Doc: N2 CallExpr-only bound moved onto `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding` (N6).\\n- FINDING (measured): weakened guard `major > math.MaxInt/10` wraps 922337203685477580802.0.0 to major 2 (exit 13, aliasing native 2) while shipped saturates to MaxInt (exit 6); token-preserving inserts (`if digit == ':' { continue }`, `if rest[i] == '/' { continue }`, plus the '/' -in-major and ':'-in-rest mirrors) leave the derived arm set byte-identical (bijection 167/167) and survived the whole suite; peek widening `recognized || ...` slides bare-frame member `ok` to `protocol_version` with code/exit unchanged. All now redden behaviourally.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round4.md` on the board task (F1a/F1b tables, 22-mutant battery with behavioural-vs-census split per arm, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`); battery script `mut_round4.py` + `battery-round4-all.json` under repo-root `.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/`.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 85.8%, terminalbackend 94.2%), `go vet` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 98 acceptance cases). Battery: 22 applied / 21 killed / 1 survived (M12 declared equivalent per N5) + NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL as distinct control rows; all 4 token-preserving killed behaviourally with zero census kill.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2252 — review round 3: saturation short-circuit reclassified malformed versions (G1)\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (G1 blocking + N1–N3 notes; F1/F2/F4/F5 and the F3 rewrite stand as the reviewer verified them and were not re-litigated). Production: `provhost/protocol.go` `parseMajor` only — the saturating early `return math.MaxInt, true` is now `major = math.MaxInt; continue`, so an overflowing first component still saturates but the minor/patch shape check always runs. Doc paragraph narrowed to what the code enforces (only a fully numeric X.Y.Z reports a recognized major). Tests: new `TestParseMajorSaturationStillValidatesTheRest` (5 giant-malformed rows assert `parseMajor` unrecognized AND `DecodeResponse` provider_protocol_error/exit 13 through the production entry).\\n- FINDING (measured through `DecodeResponse`, pre-fix probe): `99999999999999999999.abc.def`, `99999999999999999999.0.x`, `18446744073709551618..0` classified `incompatible_protocol`/exit 6 while `2.abc.def` classified `provider_protocol_error`/exit 13 — a plugin chose the refusal class and exit status, and the whole provhost suite passed identically on both behaviors (effect census, not branch census: the parse-arm census enumerates rejection branches and cannot see inputs moving between existing arms). Post-fix measurement: all-numeric giants (`18446744073709551618.0.0`, `99999999999999999999.0.0`) stay `incompatible_protocol`/exit 6 — that 13→6 shift is the intended, still-measured F2 effect; every malformed-rest giant is back to exit 13.\\n- CORRECTION: the round-2 outcome sentence \\\"no gate was weakened … parse-arm census derives the identical set\\\" is withdrawn as classification-stability evidence in `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round3.md`; the census claim survives only in its scoped form (saturation adds no `return 0, false` branch, so the inventory needs no new row). AC ratio corrected to 14 of 15 driven + 1 stated bound (row 14, F6 future-caller prose). N2 bound stated: the attestation tripwire matches `CallExpr` only, so a function-value binding would be missed (0 such references today). Battery scripts live at repo-root `.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/` (N3).\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round3.md` on the board task (G1 table, corrected arm-shift sentence, 14+1 AC ratio, 8-mutant battery table); battery script `mutG1_round3.py` + `mutsG1_round3.json` under repo-root `.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/`.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-race` provider/provhost/terminalbackend exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 85.8%, terminalbackend 94.2%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok (60 c